\par\par \b \uc2 *S&PGR Revises \uc2 Telekom Malaysia\uc2  'A-' FC Rtg Otlk To Stbl\b0\par\par\uc2 1,642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2022\par 07:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 28 Jun 2022 01:31 ET  Press Release: S&PGR Revises \uc2 Telekom Malaysia\uc2   'A-' FC Rtg Otlk To Stbl\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from S&P Global Ratings: \par  \par      -- On June 27, 2022, S&P Global Ratings revised the outlook on its \par sovereign ratings on Malaysia to stable from negative, while affirming the \par 'A-/A-2' foreign and 'A/A-1' local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings. \par      -- We revised the outlook on the long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issuer credit \par rating on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  . to stable from negative while affirming our \par 'A-' long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on the company and on its senior \par unsecured notes. \par      -- We affirmed our 'A-' long-term local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom \par Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2   with a stable outlook. \par      -- The stable outlook mirrors the outlook on the sovereign rating on \par Malaysia, and our view that the credit profile of the Malaysia-based \par fixed-line operator is intrinsically linked due to its relationship with the \par government. \par  \par SINGAPORE (S&P Global Ratings) June 28, 2022--S&P Global Ratings today took \par the rating actions listed above. \par  \par We revised the outlook on our foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issuer credit ratings on \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2   to stable from negative following a similar rating action on \par the Malaysia sovereign credit rating (foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  A-/Stable/A-2; local \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  A/Stable/A-1). \par  \par The company's performance will likely remain sensitive, to some extent, to \par government policies. This is given the government's majority ownership in the \par company--including government-related shareholders, the Malaysian government \par owns more than 60% of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  . The government also owns a special \par share in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2   via the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Incorporated), which \par enables it to ensure \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  's direction is in line with government \par policies. Furthermore, the government had previously \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to improve \par connectivity in the country at the expense of the company's near-term \par earnings. We believe the risk of such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will persist in the \par medium-term because \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   will remain instrumental to the \par government's intent to improve broadband speed and coverage in the country. \par  \par The stable outlook on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2   reflects our view that the company will \par remain the dominant fixed-line player in Malaysia and maintain its \par debt-to-EBITDA below 2.5x over the next 12-24 months. \par  \par We may lower the rating if \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  's debt-to-EBITDA ratio moves to \par 2.5x. This could happen if (1) its competitive position or operating \par performance deteriorate materially because of heightened competition or \par regulatory pressures; or (2) the company's capital spending or shareholder \par distributions are much higher than we anticipate. \par  \par We may also lower our ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2   if we lower the sovereign \par ratings on Malaysia. \par  \par We may revise \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  's stand-alone credit profile upward if: (1) the \par company maintains its operating performance and adopts a conservative \par financial policy, as reflected in the ratio of debt to EBITDA staying close to \par 1.5x on a sustained basis; or (2) the company significantly improves its \par market position in the wireless segment while maintaining a debt-to-EBITDA \par ratio of about 2x. \par  \par The long-term ratings remain constrained by the sovereign foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par rating. \par  \par ESG credit indicators: E-2, S-2, G-2 \par  \par RELATED CRITERIA \par  \par      -- General Criteria: Environmental, Social, And Governance Principles In \par Credit Ratings, Oct. 10, 2021 \par      -- General Criteria: Group Rating Methodology, July 1, 2019 \par      -- Criteria | Corporates | General: Corporate Methodology: Ratios And \par Adjustments, April 1, 2019 \par      -- Criteria | Corporates | General: Reflecting Subordination Risk In \par Corporate Issue Ratings, March 28, 2018 \par      -- General Criteria: Rating Government-Related Entities: Methodology And \par Assumptions, March 25, 2015 \par      -- Criteria | Corporates | General: Methodology And Assumptions: \par Liquidity Descriptors For Global Corporate Issuers, Dec. 16, 2014 \par      -- Criteria | Corporates | Industrials: Key Credit Factors For The \par Telecommunications And Cable Industry, June 23, 2014 \par      -- General Criteria: Country Risk Assessment Methodology And Assumptions, \par Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Criteria | Corporates | General: Corporate Methodology, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- General Criteria: Methodology: 