\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Thai baht firms on cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  doubts,  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  shares climb\b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2020\par 06:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (.)\par     * Indonesian markets closed for a holiday\par     * Baht hovers near key support level\par     * Malaysia's Public Bank announces bonus share issue\par \par     By Anushka Trivedi\par     Dec 9 (Reuters) - The Thai baht hit a near one-year high on\par Wednesday as traders sold dollars amid expectations that \f28 \uc2 \f2 the\par Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rapid\par rise, while Malaysian equities jumped more than 1%, lifted by\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The baht firmed 0.2% to 30.04 against the dollar\par and has now recouped most of its losses made this year since a\par breakthrough in coronavirus vaccine in November brightened the\par outlook for the trade and tourism-reliant Thai economy.\par     The Bangkok index is on track to gain over 2% in two\par sessions after the country eased curbs on tourist arrivals,\par while foreign equity inflows have added to the baht's strength,\par which Thai exporters on Tuesday urged the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb\par at 30.0 per dollar mark.\par     "There was 'panic USD selling' among exporters once baht\par rose beyond 30.15 on expecting support from Bank of Thailand ...\par and given no \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  briefing by BoT as previously expected,\par some exporters may be in wait and see mode and could rush to\par sell dollars more once baht rises above 30 level," said Poon\par Panichpibool, markets strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which cancelled a planned briefing on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures, may not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at this level but could use\par unconventional tools like quantitative easing as well as debt\par monetisation to limit the baht's gains, Poon added.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose against a softer greenback\par , with the Taiwanese dollar leading gains at 1%\par stronger.\par     However, the Indian rupee failed to capitalise,\par dropping 0.1%, on suspicions the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par mopping up inflows to prevent its rise.\par     In the equity markets, Malaysia's index scaled a\par 16-month peak after the country's second-largest lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public\par Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced a bonus share issue, which\par brokerage MIDF Research said would improve the bank's liquidity\par and the stock's affordability.\par     Positive sentiment from a strong finish at Wall Street on\par progress in coronavirus vaccines spilled over to Asia as most\par stock markets made big gains.\par     South Korea's KOSPI rose 1.4% and Singapore shares\par  advanced 0.6%.\par     Financial markets in Indonesia were shut due to a public\par holiday.\par  \par     HIGHLIGHTS\par         \par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 8.9%, its highest since Jan.\par 7\par     ** Thailand's 10-year government bond yields are down 1.5\par basis points at 1.265%\par     \par \par   Asia stock indexes and                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at   0453 GMT                                                 \par  COUNTRY    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DAILY %    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YTD %     INDEX  STOCKS DAILY %  STOCKS YTD %\par  Japan                       +0.02       +4.30                      1.15         13.17\par  China                       +0.10       +6.70                      0.06         11.87\par  India                       -0.08       -2.99                      0.58         10.70\par  Malaysia                    +0.15       +0.62                      0.96          3.69\par  Philippin                   +0.23       +5.41                     -0.66         -8.43\par  es                                                                       \par  S.Korea                     +0.33       +6.90                      1.55         24.80\par  Singapore                   +0.23       +0.75                      0.57        -11.83\par  Taiwan                      +1.05       +6.68                      0.25         19.99\par  Thailand                    +0.17       -0.27                      0.03         -6.36\par  \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par  (Editing by Stephen Coates)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-9T06:29:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201209egc900jr5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
