\par\par \b \uc2 SE Asia Stocks-Philippines, Indonesia rise as U.S., China allay trade war fears\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2019\par 06:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Thailand nearly flat as energy, banking stocks drag\par     * Indonesia snaps four sessions of losses\par \par     By Soumyajit Saha\par     Aug 7 (Reuters) - Philippine and Indonesian shares gained\par more than 1% Wednesday, after Beijing and Washington stepped up\par to ease escalating trade war tensions, while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par dragged down by consumer stocks.    \par     Chinese authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to steady the yuan on Tuesday\par after letting it slide to its lowest in over a decade on the\par previous day, which had sparked accusations of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par manipulation from the United States and threatened to spread the\par trade war into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  space.\par     U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  then played down fears of a\par protraction in the trade war, tweeting that "massive amounts of\par money from China and other parts of the world" were coming into\par the U.S. economy.\par     "Acceleration towards an all-out trade war between the U.S.\par and China appears to have been averted, at least for the\par moment," said Stephen Innes, managing partner at VM Markets Pte\par Ltd. \par     Real estate and banking stocks pushed up Philippine's\par benchmark more than 1%. Property developer SM Prime\par Holdings rose 1.7%, while lender BDO Unibank advanced\par 1.4%.\par     Philippines' trade deficit narrowed as imports fell 10.4%,\par while exports grew 1.5%.\par     The banking sector helped Indonesian shares gain,\par with lenders \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Central Asia\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Rakyat\par Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Persero) rising 1.6% each.\par     Meanwhile, the Malaysian index fell, hurt by losses\par in the consumer cyclical sector.\par     Tourism company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genting Malaysia Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  and related\par group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genting Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 10.8% and 5.3%, respectively,\par after Genting Malaysia decided to acquire and privatise the\par loss-making \f28 \uc2 \f2 Empire Resorts Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .  \par     Thai stocks also edged marginally lower, hurt by\par losses in the energy and banking sectors.\par     Lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Ayudhya\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 1.3%, while oil\par explorer \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTT Exploration and Production\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 1.2%.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to hold its\par benchmark rate steady in a meeting later today, a Reuters poll\par showed, despite slowing growth and easing moves by its regional\par peers.\par     Energy stocks were also hurt by the a drop in oil prices\par overnight, as escalating trade war fears had ignited worries\par over demand.\par  \par For Asian Companies click;  \par \par SOUTHEAST ASIAN STOCK MARKETS as on 0408 GMT\par  STOCK MARKETS                                    \par  Change on the day                                \par  Market                 Current   Previous close  Pct Move\par  Singapore              3173.22   3170.47         0.09\par  Bangkok                1671.38   1671.48         -0.01\par  Manila                 7846.92   7766.75         1.03\par  Jakarta                6207.327  6119.471        1.44\par  Kuala Lumpur           1605.22   1611.79         -0.41\par  Ho Chi Minh            966.63    964.61          0.21\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2019                            \par  Market  