\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia's Mahathir proposes common East Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  pegged to gold\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2019\par 07:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR, May 30 (Reuters) - Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad on Thursday mooted the idea of a common trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for East Asia that would be pegged to gold, describing the existing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in the region as manipulative.\par \par \uc2 Mahathir said the proposed common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be used to settle imports and exports, but would not be used for domestic transactions.\par \par \uc2 "In the Far East, if you want to come together, we should start with a common trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not to be used locally but for the purpose of settling of trade," he said at the Nikkei Future of Asia conference in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we propose should be based on gold because gold is much more stable."\par \par \uc2 He said under the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were affected by external factors and were manipulated. He did not elaborate on how they were manipulated.\par \par \uc2 Mahathir has long been a critic of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, and once famously accused billionaire \uc2 George Soros\uc2  of betting against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the Asian financial crisis, Mahathir pegged the ringgit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 3.8 to the dollar and imposed capital controls. That peg was scrapped in 2005.\par \par \uc2 Mahathir served a 22-year term as prime minister before stepping down in 2003. He was re-elected in May last year in a shock election, defeating the Barisan Nasional coalition that had ruled Malaysia for the six decades since independence.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the Trump administration said no major trading partner met the criteria required to be placed on the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2 's list of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators but named Malaysia among nine countries that required close scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 In response, \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was limited to managing excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rozanna Latiff, writing by A. Ananthalakshmi; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-30T06:19:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190530ef5u00kix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
