\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia Vote Shocks Investors -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By WSJ Staff \par \uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2018\par 08:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par B11\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 This article is being republished as part of our daily reproduction of WSJ.com articles that also appeared in the U.S. print edition of The Wall Street Journal (May 11, 2018).\par \par \uc2 Heavy selling looms in Malaysian assets when markets reopen next week, after the country's opposition coalition pulled off a shock victory in Wednesday's election.\par \par \uc2 A U.S.-listed exchange-traded fund of Malaysian stocks slumped 6% on Wednesday, its biggest decline since 2011, while the dollar has risen more than 2% against the ringgit in the derivatives market.\par \par \uc2 Incoming Malaysian prime minister \uc2 Mahathir Mohamad\uc2  earlier declared two days of national holidays after his Alliance of Hope coalition secured a parliamentary majority following the vote in the Southeast Asian nation.\par \par \uc2 The "huge upset" over \uc2 Najib Razak\uc2  "ranks up there with Brexit and [U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's] election," said Aninda Mitra, senior sovereign analyst at BNY Mellon Investment Management.\par \par \uc2 While anticipating short-term volatility in Malaysian markets next week, "a long-term fix of governance, institutions and public life is now in sight," he said. Still, he added, near-term policy uncertainty will be high, taking a toll on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ringgit, for now.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks had started falling ahead of the election, as signs emerged that Dr. Mahathir's opposition party was gaining momentum. His party has offered few details on its economic policy plans, although its campaign manifesto proposed scrapping the country's goods-and-services tax and reintroducing fuel subsidies.\par \par \uc2 Such moves could have a negative impact on Malaysia's credit rating without offsetting measures to raise fiscal revenues, \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  warned in a statement Thursday. It currently rates the country at A3, four steps above the investment-grade rating threshold.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's election upset comes at a time of heightened stress in global emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Argentina has tapped the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  for financial backing, the latest drastic step policy makers have taken as they seek to stem the peso's depreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week boosted interest rates to 40%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Turkey's markets have continued to swoon over concerns about its economy. Standard & Poor's Global Ratings recently slashed the country's sovereign-debt rating further into junk territory, and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  has warned that Turkey's economy is at risk of overheating.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's neighbor Indonesia has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks to shore up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah, while foreign investors have been running from its stocks and bonds. Markets there are closed Thursday for the Ascension Day holiday.\par \par \uc2 Investors had been positive on Malaysia's market at the start of 2018, with the ringgit and equities outperforming regional peers: The country's main stock benchmark briefly topped its 2014 record high last month.\par \par \uc2 However, the ongoing corruption scandal surrounding Mr. Najib and state-owned investment fund \uc2 1Malaysia Development Bhd\uc2 ., which is subject to investigations in multiple countries, has clouded investor sentiment.\par \par \uc2 The yield on a 10-year bond from 1MDB that matures in 2023 surged to 9.54% on Thursday morning, according to \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2 , up from 6.1% on Wednesday. Bond yields rise when their prices fall.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring Malaysian government debt has also risen, with the price of 5-year credit default swaps up nearly 9% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian election results also weighed on neighboring Singapore's stock market. Equities there had been underperforming of late -- with Malaysia -- and the Straits Times Index was lower most of the day, though little changed heading into the last hour of trading Thursday amid broad gains for Asia-Pacific stock indexes.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  went ahead with its previously scheduled policy meeting and as expected kept interest rates at 3.25%.\par \par \uc2 The policy statement only had one mention of the election.\par \par \uc2 "The domestic economic outlook remains positive, the financial sector is strong and monetary and financial conditions are supportive of economic growth in the post-election environment," it said. That could signal \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confidence that the markets can weather uncertainties created by the change in government.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 11, 2018 02:32 ET (06:32 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180511ee5b000z9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
