\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Soft yuan dampens Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; Turkish lira recovers some losses\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2016\par 07:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan at new 5-1/2-yr low; suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par limits\par     * Ringgit down on upbeat U.S. economic data; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds\par up\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 18 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on Monday as China's yuan hit a more than\par 5-1/2-year trough after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its daily guidance\par rate at its lowest since October 2010 with the dollar firm after\par upbeat U.S. economic data.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of emerging Asian countries had a muted reaction\par to the failed coup in Turkey as the authorities over the weekend\par foiled the attempt by some in the military to overthrow the\par government. The Turkish lira jumped as much as 2.4\par percent in thin Asian trade on Monday, after falling nearly 5\par percent on Friday following news of the coup bid.\par     The yuan fell to 6.9998 per dollar, its weakest\par since November 2010, before state-run banks were suspected of\par selling dollars on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 6.6996 to\par support the renminbi. \par     Such weakness dragged South Korea's won,\par Singapore's dollar and Malaysia's ringgit \par weaker.\par     "Once the yuan breaches a critical point of 6.7, it will be\par difficult for other emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ignore that,"\par said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures research head in Seoul.\par     "That will spur caution on further strength in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been enjoying capital inflows\par on expectations that global central banks may ease monetary\par policies to support their economies in the wake of Britain's\par vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  last month.\par     The renminbi held a more bearish tone among regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as China's authorities were seen allowing further\par weakness. Policy sources told Reuters in June that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's\par Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  would tolerate a fall in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to as weak\par as 6.8 in 2016 to support struggling exporters. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slid amid low trading volume as traders cut some\par of their bullish bets on the U.S. dollar's broad strength.\par     The greenback held firm against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as strong U.S. retail sales and industrial production\par caused investors to price in more odds of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par interest rate hike this year. \par     "It is better to see if U.S. rate-hike talks resurface,"\par said a senior Malaysian bank trader in Kuala Lumpur.\par     Chances for a rate increase by December rose to 46 percent\par on Friday, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's FedWatch tool. Traders had\par priced in less than a 20-percent chance as recently as late\par June.\par     Still, the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its earlier\par losses as most government bond prices rose.\par     \par     WON\par     The won eased on caution that South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities may not allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen past a\par chart resistance area between 1,133 per dollar and 1,128.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered some of its earlier\par losses as foreign investors continued to buy Seoul shares\par .\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0450 GMT    \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par  *Japan yen                   105.45         104.92     -0.50\par   Sing dlr                    1.3488         1.3470     -0.13\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.970         31.990     +0.06\par   Korean won                 1136.30        1133.90     -0.21\par  *Baht                         34.93          34.93      0.00\par   Peso                        46.830         46.800     -0.06\par   Rupiah                       13100          13090     -0.08\par   Rupee                        67.12          67.06     -0.09\par   Ringgit                     3.9750         3.9475     -0.69\par   Yuan                        6.6974         6.6883     -0.14\par                                                              \par   Change so far in 2016                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   105.45         120.30    +14.08\par   Sing dlr                    1.3488         1.4177     +5.11\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.970         33.066     +3.43\par   Korean wo