\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up on hopes Britain will vote to stay in EU\b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2016\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan edges up; \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixes midpoint stronger\par     * Won near 2-wk high on exporters; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution caps\par     * Ringgit gains on higher \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond prices\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 21 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled ahead on Tuesday amid growing expectations\par that Britons may vote to remain in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  in this\par week's referendum, while trading was subdued on sustained risks\par of an exit.\par     China's yuan edged up on the dollar's \par broad weakness and as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its daily guidance\par rate firmer. \par     The South Korean won rose to a near two-week high\par on exporters' demand for settlements. The Malaysian ringgit\par  advanced, tracking higher bond prices.\par     Two of the latest polls suggested more British voters\par preferred to remain in the EU, helping improve global risk\par sentiment. \par     "More investors seemed to reflect possibilities of\par 'Bremain'. If they decide to stay, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will rally\par as Brexit has been the only hurdle to their appreciation,\par especially given the Fed's recent stance," said Yuna Park,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at Dongbu Securities in Seoul.\par     "Still, it is difficult to make direction bets either way\par now."\par     Last week, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  said slower economic\par growth would crimp the pace of monetary policy tightening in\par future years, although it signalled plans to raise interest\par rates twice this year. Investors were awaiting Fed\par Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 's testimony before the Senate Banking\par Committee later on Tuesday.\par     \par     WON\par     The won gained 0.4 percent to 1,156.0 per dollar, its\par strongest since June 9.\par     South Korea posted a trade surplus of $3.9 billion during\par the first 20 days of June, according to Reuters calculations\par based on data from Customs Korea data. \par     Sentiment remained fragile with the won briefly weaker in\par thin trading on dollar demand from foreign investors, which\par traders suspected were linked to stocks outflows.\par     Possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the won's strength was also\par keeping investors wary after authorities were suspected of\par selling the won in overnight offshore markets and in the\par domestic market on Monday, traders said.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose 0.3 percent to 4.0500 per dollar, its\par strongest since June 10.\par     Malaysia's government bond prices rose with the 5-year yield\par  at 3.48 percent, its lowest since June 9.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders took profits around the ringgit's session\par high on caution ahead of the British vote on Thursday.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0415 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   103.99         103.92     -0.07\par   Si