\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-Battered Indonesian rupiah, Malaysia ringgit stage strong rally\b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2015\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to remove repeated words in paragraph three)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon and Gayatri Suroyo\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE/JAKARTA, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Asia's worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indonesian rupiah and Malaysian ringgit, rallied strongly to multi-week highs on Wednesday, helped by the previous day's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Indonesian authorities, robust Malaysian data and a heavy liquidation of positions.\par \par \uc2 By close of Asian trading, the ringgit had risen nearly 5 percent against the dollar to levels around 4.16 per dollar. The rupiah had risen 7 percent over two days to 13,700 per dollar. On Sept. 29, both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fallen to more than 17 years lows, striking levels unseen since the Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 "Rupiah and ringgit rebounded the most because they are more oversold than other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region," said Heng Koon How, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse Private Bank and Wealth Management in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Heng said there were two reasons for the broad recovery in emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , namely the rebound in oil prices and market expectations for the first U.S. interest rate rise in years being pushed out after last week's weak jobs data.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's stock market too was among top gainers in the region on Wednesday as a jump in oil prices propped up refiners and mining stocks. U.S. crude oil rose more than $1 to $49.64 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 Besides the hope this rally in crude oil will push up prices for Malaysia's exports of liquified natural gas, the ringgit also enjoyed a reprieve from the past weeks of relentless selling pressure after data showed a big jump in the August trade surplus.\par \par \uc2 Even after Wednesday's rally, the ringgit is down 16 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 While Malaysia's economic outlook looks better on the back of the oil price recovery, improved exports and the Trans-Pacific trade deal, Prime Minister \uc2 Najib Razak\uc2 's political prospects remained mired in the scandal over allegations of graft and mismanagement at indebted state fund \uc2 1Malaysia Development Berhad\uc2  (1MDB).\par \par \uc2 "More such sizable trade surpluses could help investors conclude that the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness was beginning to have a salutary impact on trade, suggesting perhaps that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness was overdone," Siddharth Mathur, head of emerging Asia strategy at Citi, said.\par \par \uc2 Mathur however said investors would still be looking to sell the ringgit on rallies until the political situation improved and thin trading volumes in the spot market meant there could be volatility and large moves in either direction.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's royal rulers weighed in on the controversy on Tuesday, with a strongly worded statement.\par \par \uc2 The sultans of nine states and governors of the remaining four said the government's failure to give convincing answers on 1MDB may have resulted in a "crisis of confidence" and asked for the government to quickly conclude investigations and take appropriate action against those implicated, the Bernama news agency reported.\par \par \uc2 RESERVES RUNNING DOWN\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's rupiah has mainly been ground down by worries foreigners who hold more than a third of its high-yielding government bonds will pull their money out as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  starts raising rates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 , has announced measures to contain the weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which at its weakest levels earlier this month was at lows last seen during the Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Traders suspected those measures, particularly its plan to supply dollars in the forward markets, were behind the rupiah's recovery this week. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's deputy governor Mirza Adityaswara said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have helped improve the supply of dollars but he denied \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Both central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesia have been conscious of their precarious \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves positions and spot market dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been rare.\par \par \uc2 Data on Wednesday showed Indonesia's reserves were down to $101.7 billion at the end of September, having shed nearly $14 billion since they peaked in February.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's reserves were down to $93.3 billion at the end of September, falling $2 billion in the second half of the month, and $34 billion less than they were a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Vidya Ranganathan; Additional reporting by Yantoultra Ngui in Kuala Lumpur; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-7T12:15:10.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151007eba700dxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
