\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. payrolls caution consigns Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to weekly losses, ringgit weak\b0\par\par\uc2 986 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2015\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Repeats to fix formatting in lead paragraph)\par     * Malaysia c.bank to release \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves data at 1000 GMT\par     * Ringgit leads Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weekly slides\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par eased on Friday and were on course for weekly losses as\par investors grew cautious ahead of U.S. jobs data that might yield\par clues on the likelihood of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  raising interest\par rates this month.\par     The Malaysian ringgit weakened most, as a political\par scandal continued to fray investor confidence in the wake of\par large-scale anti-government demonstrations last weekend.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves data due to be released later in\par the day may reveal the extent of the pressures on Asia's\par worst-performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year.\par     Otherwise, markets everywhere were focused on August U.S.\par nonfarm payrolls data later in the day.\par      A solid number could ease worries about sluggish global\par growth, and support risk sentiment, though at the same time it\par would reinforce expectations tha the Fed will move soon, which\par would hurt risk assets including emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Prospects of the Fed's September liftoff eased on the recent\par turmoil sparked in global markets by China's tumbling stocks and\par  fears of hard landing in the world's second-largest economy.\par     Some economists said the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will need to see\par much stronger jobs numbers if it is to raise rates this month\par for the first time since 2006. \par     Economists polled by Reuters expect the U.S. economy created\par 220,000 new non-farm jobs last month, while average hourly\par earnings are predicted to have risen by a modest 0.2 percent as\par they did in July.\par     Regardless of the timing of U.S. tightening, emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to stay weak, analysts said.\par     "Given continuing China concerns, volatile commodity prices\par and capital outflows, any respite for EM assets looks decidedly\par fragile and any benefit from a delay in Fed hikes is likely to\par be limited," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' analysts said in a note.\par     China's economic data in coming weeks may indicate a further\par slowdown with export and import numbers due on Tuesday likely\par continue to shrink. China is the largest trading\par partner to most emerging Asian countries.\par     \par     MALAYSIA RESERVES\par     The ringgit led weekly losses among regional units with a\par 1.6 percent slide against the dollar so far this week, Thomson\par Reuters data showed.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will announce international reserves\par as of end-August at 1000 GMT. The reserves fell to $94.5 billion\par as of Aug. 14, the lowest since September 2009, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par showed last month. \par     In August, the ringgit lost 9 percent, more than a half of\par this year's depreciation.\par     "We expect August to have ended with a big outflow of\par reserves," ING said.   \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the\par ringgit's weakness as confidence shrank partially due to a\par corruption scandal swirling round Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  and\par indebted state fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 1Malaysia Development Berhad\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The South Korean won has slid 1.5 percent\par throughout this week as foreign investors kept selling Seoul\par shares. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under further pressure from\par expectations of rising dollar demand linked to corporate merger\par deals.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 CJ Korea Express Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 , South Korea's largest\par logistics company, said it is in final talks to acquire China's\par Rokin Logistics, submitting a bid of a little above 500 billion\par won ($419.4 million). \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tesco\f28 \uc2 \f2  has picked Seoul-based private equity firm\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 MBK Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  as preferred bidder to buy its South Korean unit\par for as much as $6.6 billion, sources said. \par     Indonesia's rupiah has fallen 1.5 percent so far\par this week as falling commodity prices boosted concerns over the\par economic fundamentals of the major exporter of coal and crude\par palm oil.\par     The Singapore dollar has slid 0.6 percent for the\par week, while the Indian rupee has eased 0.3 percent.\par     By contrast, the Chinese yuan gained 0.5 percent\par in the holiday-shortened week on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts to\par stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after its devaluation on Aug. 11.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  will tighten rules on trading of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forwards from October, sources with direct knowledge of\par the matter told Reuters, in a move to curb speculation against\par the renminbi. The authorities were also spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness, traders said.\par     Other regional central banks were also suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but they were still\par weaker than levels before the China's devaluation.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0510 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.43         120.10       +0.56\par   Sing dlr        1.4178         1.4165       -0.09\par   Taiwan dlr      32.566         32.801       +0.72\par   Korean won     1191.70        1190.30       -0.12\par   Baht             35.84          35.84       +0.01\par   Peso             46.74          46.73       -0.02\par   Rupiah        14188.00       14168.00       -0.14\par   Rupee            66.38          66.24       -0.20\par   Ringgit         4.2600         4.2455       -0.34\par  *Yuan            6.3559         6.3559       +0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.43         119.66       +0.19\par   Sing dlr        1.4178         1.3260       -6.47\par   Taiwan dlr      32.566         31.718       -2.60\par   Korean won     1191.70        1099.30       -7.75\par   Baht             35.84          32.90       -8.19\par   Peso             46.74          44.72       -4.32\par 