\par\par \b \uc2 USD/MYR May Breach Key 4.0000 Round-Figure Barrier -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 03:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0105 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR remains buoyant, a day after the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  stunned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with a one-off devaluation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/MYR is fast approaching the 4.0000 round-figure trading barrier - which if breached could trigger an avalanche of stoploss orders and momentum-based buying by algorithmic trading funds. The barrier may be protected by the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so as to avoid a steep and sudden fall in the ringgit's value, but dwindling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - due to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - will encourage punters to test \uc2 Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to defend the ringgit. The USD/MYR offshore market turned exceptionally bullish Tuesday after the yuan devaluation, with the price premium of the 1-month nondeliverable forward contract rising to 600 pips above that of the spot contract, whereas it was trading at around 200 pips above on Monday.\par \par \uc2  This gauge is a useful indicator of speculative pressure on USD/MYR, which now trades at 3.9950 from its Tuesday close of 3.9600. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 11, 2015 21:05 ET (01:05 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c00018\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\