\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yuan slides drive Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to multi-year lows on China devaluation\b0\par\par\uc2 951 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2015\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan to see largest daily loss\par     * Singapore dlr, Taiwan dlr Philippine peso hit 5-year lows\par     * Ringgit, rupiah touch 17-year troughs\par     * Won near 3-year low; S.Korea not worried about won slide\par \par  (Adds details, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 11 (Reuters) - China's yuan headed for its\par largest daily loss and drove emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par multi-year lows on Tuesday after Beijing surprisingly devalued\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , building up expectations that its neighbours may\par follow a similar path to prop up exports.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  weakened the yuan,\par guiding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to its lowest point in almost three years,\par dropping by nearly 2 percent in early trade. \par  \par     The move came after China's exports in July slumped more\par than expected, while producer prices hit a six-year low.\par  \par     "China is acknowledging that a strong yuan is hurting\par exporters," said Sean Yokota, head of Asia strategy for\par Scandinavian bank SEB in Singapore.\par     The move is likely to put more pressure on other emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as central banks may allow their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par weaken amid slowing regional growth, Yokota said.\par     Some regional central banks such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par have been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem weakness in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid\par growing expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise\par interest rates this year.\par     "They don't want rapid weakness but if your \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par weakening together with your trading partners, it shouldn't be a\par problem," Yokota said.\par     A South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official told Reuters that\par Seoul is not overly worried about any weakening in the won after\par the China's devaluation as long as the won moves in an orderly\par manner. \par     The Singapore dollar and the Taiwan dollar \par hit five-year lows on the news.\par     Malaysia's ringgit and Indonesia's rupiah fell\par to lows last seen during the Asian financial crisis 17 year ago.\par     The Philippine peso also slid to a five-year low,\par while the South Korean won turned weaker to hover\par around a three-year trough.\par     "We need to stress that there is urgent need to hedge Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk. This is not just a case of USD strength ahead of the\par Fed rate hike, but also weak domestic drivers," said Heng Koon\par How, Credit Suisse Private Bank's senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist.\par     "Today's 2 percent depreciation of the CNY adds to the\par urgency and volatile mix."\par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar fell as much as 1.3 percent to 1.3996\par per the U.S. dollar, its weakest since July 2010.\par     The city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely tracks the yuan as traders\par and analysts believe it is included in the undisclosed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par basket used by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  to manage \par monetary policy.\par     Singapore downgraded its 2015 economic growth forecast as\par economists said the outlook stays tepid in the second half,\par given risks to global economic prospects. \par     The Singapore dollar pared some of its earlier losses with a\par large option barrier at 1.4000, traders said.\par     \par     WON\par     The won started the day firmer and strengthend to a session\par high of 1,155.4 per dollar on the greenback's broad weakness in\par overnight markets.\par     The South Korean won turned sharply weaker after the China's\par devaluation to hit 1,179.0 per dollar, its weakest since June\par 2012.\par     Offshore investors including real money accounts and macro\par funds scrambled to buy dollars against the won, prompting\par traders to cover short positions in the dollar, traders said.\par     Traders in Seoul suspected the local authorities of selling\par dollars to tame the won's volatility as its daily movement of\par 23.3 won per dollar was the largest since Dec. 19 2011.\par     Still, offshore funds continued to sell the won as the\par authorities were not seen excessively concerned over the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit lost 0.7 percent to 3.9550 per U.S. dollar, its\par weakest since Sept. 2 1998, the day before Malaysia pegged it at\par 3.8000 per dollar to put a floor under the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the\par Asian crisis.\par     Malaysia took the ringgit off the peg in 2005.\par     Government bond prices continued to fall, a sign that\par investors are losing confidence in Malayasia due to some\par political uncertainty and low commodity prices.\par     The five-year bond yield rose to 3.860 percent, \par highest since Jan. 16. The three-year yield advanced\par to 3.360 percent, its highest since June 10.\par         \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0530 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       124.71         124.65       -0.05\par   Sing dlr        1.3980         1.3810       -1.22\par   Taiwan dlr      31.930         31.760       -0.53\par   Korean won     1176.30        1163.20       -1.11\par   Baht             35.34          35.18       -0.47\par   Peso             45.88          45.76       -0.26\par   Rupiah        13565.00       13548.00       -0.13\par   Rupee            64.11          63.87       -0.37\par   Ringgit         3.9510         3.9285       -0.57\par   Yuan            6.3230         6.2097       -1.79\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       124.71         119.66       -4.05\par   Sing dlr        1.3980         1.3260       -5.15\par   Taiwan dlr      31.930         31.718       -0.66\par   Korean won     1176.30        1099.30       -6.55\par   Baht             35.34          32.90       -6.90\par   Peso             45.88          44.72       -2.52\par   Rupiah        13565.00       12380.00       -8.74\par   Rupee            64.11          63.03       -1.68\par   Ringgit         3.9510         3.4965      -11.50\par   Yuan            6.3230         6.2040       -1.88\par  \par \par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Yena Park in SEOUL and IFR Markets'\par Catherine Tan; Editing by)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-11T07:08:18.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150811eb8b006yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\pics