\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  losses ahead of Malaysia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves, US job data\b0\par\par\uc2 949 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2015\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Malaysia government bond prices, stocks fall\par     * Ringgit is having its worst week in 8 months\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 7 (Reuters) - The ringgit hit another pre-peg\par 17-year low on Friday, hours before the release of Malaysian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves data  that will be closely watched.\par      If the reserves drop further, that could increase concern\par about how much ammunition the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has to defend the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par      Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on Friday, and will\par have weekly losses. Investors were awaiting U.S. jobs data that\par might cement expectations the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will raise\par interest rates next month.\par     The ringgit fell as much as 0.6 percent to 3.9280 per\par dollar, its weakest since Sept. 2, 1998, the day before the\par government pegged it at 3.8000 per dollar to put a floor under\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the Asian financial crisis. Malaysia lifted\par the peg in 2005.\par     Malaysia's government bond prices continued to fall amid\par declining confidence among foreign investors due to political\par fallout and low commodity prices. The five-year bond yield\par  rose to 3.742 percent, its highest since Feb. 17,\par while the ten-year yield advanced to a near\par two-month peak of 4.150 percent.\par     Caution increased over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to bolster the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year.\par The ringgit has been hurt by uncertainty about the future of\par Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  amid corruption allegations circling\par an indebted state fund, 1MDB. \par     However, investors doubt how heavily \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the country's international reserves already\par lost $5 billion to $100.5 billion in the first half of July. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will release the reserve data for the rest of July\par at 6 pm (1000 GMT).\par     "BNM is apt to stick to its previous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics of\par slowing the rate of depreciation when capital outflows or\par speculative pressures are evident, but if reserves fall toward\par USD 90 billion they are likely to 'let it go'," said analysts\par for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a client note.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  revised its ringgit forecast for the third\par quarter to 4.1000 from 3.8000.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost nearly 11 percent against\par the dollar this year as falling commodity prices spurred worries\par about exports from the country that supplies liquefied natural\par gas and palm oil.\par     \par     RINGGIT'S WORST WEEK IN 8 MONTHS\par     So far this week, the ringgit has fallen 2.6 percent, which\par would be its largest weekly loss since December 2014, Thomson\par Reuters data showed.\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were set to suffer weekly\par losses on growing expectations of a U.S. interest hike in\par September after upbeat U.S. economic data and hawkish comments\par by a Fed official.\par     The prospects, along with volatile China's stocks and a\par commodity rout, dragged foreign money out of emerging markets\par including Asia. Most regional bond yields also rose.\par     Singapore's dollar has slid 1.0 percent this week\par on growing concerns over a sluggish economy. The city-state's\par economy in the second quarter probably contracted 4.6 percent\par from the previous quarter on an annualised basis, in line with\par the government's earlier estimate, a Reuters poll showed.\par  \par     The Philippine peso has eased 0.1 percent for the\par week, while Indonesia's rupiah and Thailand's baht\par  have edged down.\par     The immediate focus is U.S. July nonfarm payrolls data later\par in the day. Economists expect the U.S. employment report to show\par 223,000 jobs were created in July.\par     A solid number will definitely hurt emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but a weak figure could support regional units for a\par short time, some analysts said.\par     Expectations of the Fed's liftoff and optimism on the U.S.\par economic recovery have been priced into the dollar's recent\par strength, they added.\par     "A disappointment may spur some controversies on a September\par hike and a short-term rebound in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Yuna\par Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     Preparing such possibilities, some emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose this week. The Indian rupee has advanced 0.5\par percent and the South Korean won gained 0.2 percent.\par     But such rebounds are unlikely last long as the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to raise borrowing costs later this year, Park\par added.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0645 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       124.77         124.73       -0.03\par  *Sing dlr        1.3858         1.3837       -0.15\par   Taiwan dlr      31.646         31.755       +0.34\par   Korean won     1166.24        1166.20       -0.00\par   Baht             35.17          35.17       -0.01\par   Peso             45.79          45.79       +0.00\par   Rupiah        13533.00       13541.00       +0.06\par   Rupee            63.81          63.77       -0.06\par   Ringgit         3.9230         3.9040       -0.48\par   Yuan            6.2097         6.2097       +0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       124.77         119.66       -4.10\par   Sing dlr        1.3858         1.3260       -4.32\par   Taiwan dlr      31.646         31.718       +0.23\par   Korean won     1166.24        1099.30       -5.74\par   Baht             35.17          32.90       -6.45\par   Peso             45.79          44.72       -2.34\par   Rupiah        13533.00       12380.00       -8.52\par   Rupee            63.81          63.03       -1.21\par   Ringgit         3.9230         3.4965      -10.87\par   Yuan            6.2097         6.2040       -0.09\par   * Financial markets in Singapore are closed for holidays and\par will be reopen on Tuesday, Aug 11.\par     \par \par  (Editing by Richa