\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Growing Sept Fed rate bets pummel Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; ringgit short positions at 7-mth high\b0\par\par\uc2 1,049 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2015\par 07:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ringgit short positions largest since early January\par     * Baht bearish bets hit 3-1/2-year high\par     * Philippine peso short positions at two-year high\par     * Yuan long positions fall on stocks rout, economy\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 6 (Reuters) - Sentiment towards emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deteriorated in the last two weeks, a Reuters\par poll showed on Thursday, as expectations grew that the U.S.\par Federal Reserve will begin raising interest rates in September.\par     Short positions on the Malaysian ringgit's hit the\par largest since early January as the country's political crisis\par deepened, according to the survey of 22 fund managers, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par traders and analysts conducted between Tuesday and Thursday.\par     The ringgit fell to 3.8935 per dollar, a level last seen\par during the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis, when the country\par subsequently pegged it to 3.8000 to the dollar.\par     Investors were losing confidence on Malaysia as political\par pressure piled up on Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  over corruption\par allegations swirling around indebted state-fund 1MDB.\par     Caution grew over the prospect of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par so far this year, but doubts also lingered over how heavily \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par Negara \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par falling.\par     Hopes for gains in China's yuan waned, with long\par positions falling to less than a third from the previous survey.\par     In the previous survey published on July 23, long positions\par in the yuan hit a one-month high as the authorities' support\par measures for the equity markets reduced share price volatility.\par But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has repeatedly vowed to keep the exchange\par rate steady. \par     Chinese stock markets skidded 14 percent in July, their\par biggest monthly loss in nearly six years, and are now down some\par 25 percent from mid-June highs.\par     Short positions on the Thai baht's rose to the \par largest since February 2012, when Reuters started including the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the positioning survey, as slowing growth caused\par capital outflows. The baht fell to a six-year low on July 31.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday left its benchmark\par interest rate steady again, indicating its belief that the\par weakening baht can aid exports and economic recovery better than\par a rate cut can. \par     Such a stance prompted foreign investors to reduce bond\par holdings which they had bought before on expectations that a\par rate cut may boost bond prices.\par     Bearish bets on the Philippine peso grew to the\par largest since August 2013 as it fell to a five-year low amid\par signs of an economic slowdown. Foreign investors were net\par sellers of local stocks in the previous four consecutive weeks,\par according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  data.\par     Philippine annual inflation slowed to a record low of 0.8\par percent in July. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will review the need to adjust\par its monetary stance at its rates meeting on Aug. 13, its\par governor said on Wednesday. \par     The Taiwan dollar's short positions rose to the\par highest since mid-December last year. The island's economic\par growth slowed to a three-year low in the second quarter on a\par collapse in exports amid weak global demand for key technology\par products. \par     Short positions in the Singapore dollar and the\par Indonesian rupiah hit the largest since mid-March.\par     Bearish bets on South Korea's won eased with\par caution over possible support by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities, but short positions still hovered around an\par eight-month high hit two weeks ago.\par     The Indian rupee's bearish bets slightly rose, but\par the sentiment was much better than other emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on hopes of a medium-term increase in limits on\par foreign investments. Falling inflation and stronger economic\par growth prospects also helped sentiment on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Atlanta Federal Reserve President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dennis Lockhart\f28 \uc2 \f2  backed\par September for the start of U.S. interest rate hikes.\par     Lockhart, a voter this year on the Federal Open Market\par Committee, told the Wall Street Journal this week that it would\par take "significant deterioration" in the U.S. economy for him to\par not support a rate hike next month. He is considered a centrist\par on the committee. \par     The poll is focused on what analysts and fund managers\par believe are the current market positions in nine Asian emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  6-Aug   -0.15  1.27  1.19  1.16  0.91  0.11  1.82  0.84  1.40\par  23-July -0.50  1.32  0.97  0.69  0.70  0.09  1.24  0.52  1.18\par  9-July  -0.13  1.09  0.38  0.78  0.56 -0.06  1.33  0.37  0.80\par  25-June -0.70  0.29  0.22  0.80  0.11 -0.26  1.10  0.30  0.57\par  11-June -0.47  0.77  0.61  1.12  0.48  0.05  1.39  0.43  0.69\par  28-May  -0.62  0.67  0.53  1.05  0.02  0.29  0.86  0.03  0.89\par  14-May  -0.45  0.11 -0.05  0.95 -0.30  0.22  0.41 -0.06  0.78\par  30-Apr  -0.48 -0.55 -0.44  0.43 -0.46 -0.18 -0.13 -0.12  0.33\par  16-Apr  -0.35  0.18  0.27  0.34  0.12 -0.59  1.08  0.02 -0.21\par  2-Apr   -0.13  0.14  0.69  0.74 -0.09 -0.51  1.09  0.13  0.14\par  19-Mar   0.46  1.10  1.48  1.33  0.53 -0.30  1.63  0.33  0.44\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BENGALURU and\par Masayuki Kitano; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-6T06:13:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150806eb86006lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
