\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Taiwan dlr lead Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains; ringgit steady near 17-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2015\par 07:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Exporters support won, Taiwan dollar\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution offsets \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cabinet reshuffle\par     * Caution grows ahead of Fed policy statement\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 29 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the\par Taiwan dollar rose on Wednesday due to month-end corporate\par demand, while caution mounted ahead of a U.S. Federal Reserve\par policy statement that could contain hints about interest rate\par increases in coming months.\par     Malaysia's ringgit spot stayed near a 17-year low\par despite a cabinet reshuffle as caution over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offset increased political\par tensions. Still, most of its non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs) weakened, indicating fragile\par sentiment among offshore investors.\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged up as losses in China's\par shares subdued after Beijing showed its determination to\par stabilise wild equity markets. The dollar also eased\par against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Investors took a breather, awaiting clues from the Fed on\par the timing and pace of an interest rate hike when the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  releases a policy statement later in the day.\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been weaker on views that the\par Fed may raise rates this year and as regional economic growth\par slowed.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may find short-term relief if\par expectations of the Fed's liftoff ease, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Emmanuel Ng said.\par     "Any specific references to global instability - China,\par Greece and commodities - within the statement may undermine the\par greenback," Ng said.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     Spot ringgit was quoted at 3.8130 per dollar by midday,\par compared with 3.8176 hit on Monday, its weakest since September\par 1998. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was pegged at 3.8000 from 1998 to 2005.\par     By contrast, the ringgit's one-month NDFs \par eased 0.2 percent to 3.8290 to the dollar. Five and 10-year\par government bond  prices fell.\par     Malaysian Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  sacked his deputy and\par four other ministers in a cabinet reshuffle on Tuesday, and\par replaced the attorney general, in a bid to stifle questions over\par a graft scandal at debt-laden state investment fund 1MDB.\par  \par     "This certainly raises the risk of further political turmoil\par should the public view the sackings as highly politically\par motivated, and may focus even more pressure on the PM," said\par Sacha Tihanyi, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for Scotiabank, said\par in a research note.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to provide "significant\par liquidity" during the political tensions to support the ringgit\par as the sentiment toward the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained bearish, Tihanyi\par said.\par     "We think it more likely that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is concerned\par with potential market panic at the breach of the former fixed\par exchange rate regime level of 3.80, and thus focused on ensuring\par that they maintained an orderly exchange rate market at that\par point."\par     The ringgit was pegged at 3.80 per dollar from 1998 to 2005.\par     Malaysia's international reserves fell to $100.5 billion as\par of July 15 from $105.5 billion as of June 30, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data\par showed earlier this month. \par     \par     WON\par     The won rose to 1,158.2 per dollar, up 0.6 percent from\par Tuesday, as exporters bought it for month-end settlements,\par causing traders to cut bearish bets on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The outlook for the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed dim on\par concerns over a slowdown in Asia's fourth-largest economy.\par     Exports in July likely declined for a seventh straight month\par on sluggish global demand, especially in China, a Reuters poll\par showed. \par     The won also faced chart resistance around 1,154-1,155 per\par dollar, analysts said.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar gained on month-end demand from exporters.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains were limited on weaker local stocks\par  and capital outflows from foreign financial\par institutions.\par     Foreigners were net sellers in the island's main stock\par exchange during the previous four straight sessions, unloading a\par combined net T$15.4 billion ($489.6 million) during the period,\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.  \par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0510 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       123.42         123.57       +0.12\par   Sing dlr        1.3639         1.3633       -0.04\par   Taiwan dlr      31.450         31.575       +0.40\par   Korean won     1157.80        1164.90       +0.61\par   Baht             34.91          34.89       -0.06\par   Peso             45.47          45.50       +0.07\par   Rupiah        13457.00       13460.00       +0.02\par   Rupee            63.90          63.91       +0.02\par   Ringgit         3.8130         3.8140       +0.03\par   Yuan            6.2089         6.2094       +0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       123.42         119.66       -3.05\par   Sing dlr        1.3639         1.3260       -2.78\par   Taiwan dlr      31.450         31.718       +0.85\par   Korean won     1157.80        1099.30       -5.05\par   Baht             34.91          32.90       -5.76\par   Peso             45.47          44.72       -1.65\par   Rupiah        13457.00       12380.00       -8.00\par   Rupee            63.90          63.03       -1.36\par   Ringgit         3.8130         3.4965       -8.30\par   Yuan            6.2089         6.2040       -0.08\par   ($1 = 31.455 Taiwan dollar)\par \par  (Additional reporting by Roger Tung in TAIPEI; Editing by)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-7-29T06:38:01.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150729eb7t00671\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
