\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  sentiment worsens on U.S. rate hike views; yuan exception\b0\par\par\uc2 1,022 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2015\par 08:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht bearish bets at 1-1/2-year high\par     * Won short positions largest since late November\par     * Singapore dollar sentiment worst in 4 months\par     * Yuan long positions hits 1-month peak\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 23 (Reuters) - Sentiment towards most\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deteriorated in the last two weeks, a\par Reuters poll showed on Thursday, as expectations grew that the\par U.S. Federal Reserve will raise interest rates as soon as\par September.\par     China's yuan bucked the trend as investors\par breathed more easily after the authorities' support measures for\par the stock market reduced share prices volatility, according to\par the survey of 20 fund managers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts conducted\par between Tuesday and Thursday.\par     Long positions in the yuan rose to the largest in one month,\par encouraged by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's consistent efforts to stabilise\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by keeping the daily guidance steady. \par     By contrast, most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reported more bearish\par bets as Fed officials including Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  expected a\par rise in U.S. interest rates this year. \par  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asian Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  also cut its 2015 and 2016 growth\par forecasts for China and the rest of Asia, hurting regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Bearish bets on the Thai baht hit the largest since\par January 2014 as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched six-year lows. A deputy\par prime minister said a weaker baht will help the country's\par exports and help boost a struggling economy more than an\par interest rate cut. \par     Still, some offshore funds expected a further rate cut,\par adding to pressure on the baht. Thai importers' dollar demand\par for month-end payments also hurt the baht.\par     Short positions on the South Korean won were the\par largest since late November as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a three-year\par low.\par     South Korea's economic growth more than halved in the second\par quarter from the previous three months to record the weakest\par expansion in six years due to a deadly virus outbreak, dry\par weather and poor exports. Offshore funds\par continued to sell the won as foreign investors retreated from\par the Seoul stock market.\par     Pessimism on the Singapore dollar was the highest\par since late March, when bearish bets stood at a six-year peak due\par to expectations of further monetary stimulus. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  in April surprised\par markets by holding off from more easing, but a subsequent,\par unexpected contraction in the economy during the second quarter\par revived speculation that the MAS will ease. \par     On Tuesday, however, the MAS doused those expectations, \par saying that the current policy settings were appropriate given\par the expectation that prices will rise by next year.\par  \par     The Philippine peso's short positions hit a\par 10-month peak. The country will likely miss its exports growth\par target of 8-10 percent this year after overseas sales contracted\par in the first five months of 2015, its trade secretary said on\par Wednesday. \par     Short positions in the Taiwan dollar rose to the\par largest since early January as the island's export orders fell\par for a third straight month in June on weak demand from China and\par other emerging markets. Foreign investors were\par net sellers in Taiwan's stock market so far this month.\par     Sentiment on the Indian rupee turned slightly\par negative, reflecting the regional falling trend.\par     The Malaysian ringgit's bearish bets eased a bit\par despite a political storm raging around Prime Minister Najib\par Razak after a Wall Street Journal report on state-fund 1MDB\par alleged that $700 million had been transferred into accounts\par held by Najib.\par     Reuters has not verified the Wall Street Journal report.\par Najib has denied taking any money for personal gain and said the\par corruption allegations are part of a malicious campaign to force\par him out of office.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support\par the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year, traders\par said. Government's bond prices also rose on foreign inflows.\par     Pessimism on the Indonesian rupiah weakened slightly\par although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a 17-year low. Indonesia's authorities\par repeated pledges to curb volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     The poll is focused on what analysts and fund managers\par believe are the current market positions in nine Asian emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  23-July -0.50  1.32  0.97  0.69  0.70  0.09  1.24  0.52  1.18\par  9-July  -0.13  1.09  0.38  0.78  0.56 -0.06  1.33  0.37  0.80\par  25-June -0.70  0.29  0.22  0.80  0.11 -0.26  1.10  0.30  0.57\par  11-June -0.47  0.77  0.61  1.12  0.48  0.05  1.39  0.43  0.69\par  28-May  -0.62  0.67  0.53  1.05  0.02  0.29  0.86  0.03  0.89\par  14-May  -0.45  0.11 -0.05  0.95 -0.30  0.22  0.41 -0.06  0.78\par  30-Apr  -0.48 -0.55 -0.44  0.43 -0.46 -0.18 -0.13 -0.12  0.33\par  16-Apr  -0.35  0.18  0.27  0.34  0.12 -0.59  1.08  0.02 -0.21\par  2-Apr   -0.13  0.14  0.69  0.74 -0.09 -0.51  1.09  0.13  0.14\par  19-Mar   0.46  1.10  1.48  1.33  0.53 -0.30  1.63  0.33  0.44\par  5-Mar    0.90  0.36  1.24  1.10  0.46 -0.64  1.34 -0.28  0.05\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BENGALURU;\par Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-7-23T07:53:27.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150723eb7n0089j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
