\par\par \b \uc2 USD/MYR Steady, Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Keeping Ringgit Weakness at Bay -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2015\par 03:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0159 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/MYR has been stable, teetering at the 3.8080 edge of the Bollinger uptrend channel, as the dollar struggles to rise against the ringgit due to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past week. The greenback, which continues to rally against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - due to U.S. rate-increase expectations - has flatlined against the Malaysia ringgit in recent days. Aside from USD-strength due to interest rate expectations, additional pressure on the ringgit may come from the recent drop in crude oil prices - due to the Iran nuclear sanctions deal - which threatens Malaysia's oil export revenues. This could have a negative impact on Malaysia's economy and its trade balance in the medium to long term. USD/MYR is now 3.8070 from its Thursday close of 3.8052. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 19, 2015 21:59 ET (01:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150720eb7k0001f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
