\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-China stock rout hits yuan sentiment; ringgit view most bearish in a month\b0\par\par\uc2 907 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2015\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan long positions hit 3-month low\par     * Ringgit bearish bets largest in one month\par     * Won bearish bets highest since late March\par     * Taiwan dollar short positions at 6-month high\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 9 (Reuters) - Bullish sentiment on China's\par yuan fell to the lowest in three months as Chinese stock markets\par plunged, while short positions on the Malaysian ringgit hit\par their largest in one month due to rising political tensions, a\par Reuters poll showed.\par     Bearish bets on most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increased as\par the savage sell-off in China and Greece's protracted debt crisis\par hurt risk sentiment, according to the survey of 16 fund managers\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts conducted between Tuesday and Thursday.\par     Chinese stocks have lost about 30 percent over the last\par three weeks. The sell-off pushed the yuan in the\par offshore market to four month-lows on Wednesday, although the\par renminbi remained stable onshore. \par     The yuan's long positions fell to their lowest during the\par last two weeks since early April, the poll showed. In the\par previous survey published on June 25, bullish bets hit a\par seven-month high. \par     Caution remained over the outlook for Chinese stocks,\par although they rebounded on Thursday after the securities\par regulator banned shareholders with large stakes in listed firms\par from selling the shares for six months.\par     The ringgit's short positions rose to their largest\par since early June as corruption allegations swirl around Prime\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Earlier this week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  briefly\par weakened past its old of 3.80 per dollar, fixed in September\par 1998 during the Asian financial crisis and scrapped in 2005.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for\par five consecutive sessions through Thursday to support the\par worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year, traders said.\par     The Wall Street Journal (WSJ) reported last week that\par investigators probing 1MDB had traced funds flowing into Najib's\par personal account. Reuters is unable to verify\par the report and Najib has denied taking any money from the\par debt-laden state fund or any other entity for personal gain.\par     The report undermined short-term positive sentiment on the\par Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  unexpectedly upgraded its\par rating outlook to "stable" from "negative". \par     Bearish bets on South Korea's won rose to their\par largest since late March as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a two-year low on\par Thursday on continuous foreign stock selling.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut the country's growth forecast on\par Thursday, while keeping interest rates steady at a record low to\par support the sluggish economy. \par     Pessimistic bets on the Taiwan dollar hit a\par seven-month peak as the island's stocks suffered on Wednesday\par their largest single-day slide in more than three years, with\par heavy foreign selling.\par     The Thai baht's short positions increased to their\par highest since late May as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a near six-year low\par on Wednesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under pressure from capital\par outflows.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weak in a bid to revive the economy by boosting exports,\par analysts said. \par     Long positions in the Indian rupee almost\par disappeared as the Chinese stock turmoil raised concerns of\par foreign fund outflows from Asian emerging markets in general. \par     Short positions on the Singapore dollar and the\par Philippine peso grew.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  poll is focused on what analysts and fund\par managers believe are the current market positions in nine Asian\par emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won,\par Singapore dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar,\par Indian rupee, Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai\par baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  9-July  -0.13  1.09  0.38  0.78  0.56 -0.06  1.33  0.37  0.80\par  25-June -0.70  0.29  0.22  0.80  0.11 -0.26  1.10  0.30  0.57\par  11-June -0.47  0.77  0.61  1.12  0.48  0.05  1.39  0.43  0.69\par  28-May  -0.62  0.67  0.53  1.05  0.02  0.29  0.86  0.03  0.89\p