\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -China stock rebound lifts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ;  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  c.bank keeps supporting ringgit\b0\par\par\uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2015\par 07:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seen around session low-traders\par     * Won up from 2-year low, foreigners keep selling stocks\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 9 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rebounded on Thursday as Chinese stocks turned higher, easing\par concerns over its market rout for now, while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ringgit\par edged up as authorities again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the\par regiona's worst-performing unit.\par     Chinese shares started the day sharply lower with CSI300\par index down more than 3 percent earlier, indicating a\par market meltdown is not over yet. The country's stocks have lost\par about 30 percent over the last three weeks.\par     But they reversed the direction as authorities continued to\par take measures. Late on Wednesday, China's securities regulator\par ordered shareholders with stakes of more than 5 percent from\par selling shares for the next six months. \par     State news agency \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xinhua\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Chinese police on Thursday\par visited the regulator to investigate clues that suggest\par "malicious" short-selling of stocks. \par     The rebound in Chinese stocks caused investors to cut\par bearish bets in emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but such position\par adjustments in regional units are unlikely to last long, given\par slowing growth, analysts said.\par     "At this point, sentiment is slightly better, but the\par Chinese stock market is really volatile," said Irene Cheung,\par senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for ANZ in Singapore.\par     "We are still having actually pretty poor economic numbers\par in Asia as a whole. It's not going to help Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . I\par would actually be still looking to buy dollar/Asia on the back\par of fundamental reasons."\par     China's consumer inflation edged up in June, but stubbornly\par weak producer prices fell again, adding to worries that the\par world's second-largest economy is not out of the woods yet,\par especially amid the stock market rout. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also downgraded its growth\par forecast for this year to 2.8 percent from 3.1 percent\par previously forecast due to the outbreak of Middle East\par Respiratory Syndrome and poor exports. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par around its session low of 3.8080 per dollar, traders said.\par     The authority has been seen keeping the ringgit firmer than\par a 16-year low of 3.8100 as corruption allegations swirl around\par Prime Minister Najib Razak, traders said.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended gains as traders covered\par short positions on the rebound in China's stocks.\par     Still, some traders sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on rallies as\par political tensions swirled over Najib and debt-laden state fund\par 1MDB\par     Investors were awaiting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy\par meeting later in the day. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is widely\par expected to keep its policy interest rate \par unchanged, but investors were keeping an eye on its stance on\par the recent market slides. \par     \par     WON\par     The won earlier fell as much as 0.3 percent to 1,140.0 per\par dollar, its weakest since July 2013, on dollar demand linked to\par recent foreign stock selling.\par     Foreigners were set to become net sellers in Seoul's main\par stock market for a fifth consecutive session. They have\par dumped more than 1.0 trillion won ($881.3 million) worth of\par shares in total during the five sessions, the Korea Exchange\par data showed.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, turned firmer as higher\par Chinese stocks caused stop-loss dollar selling among local\par traders.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0505 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.38         120.71       -0.55\par   Sing dlr        1.3507         1.3499       -0.06\par   Taiwan dlr      31.028         31.225       +0.63\par   Korean won     1135.00        1136.70       +0.15\par   Baht             33.97          33.99       +0.07\par   Peso             45.18          45.16       -0.03\par   Rupiah        13340.00       13340.00       +0.00\par   Rupee            63.54          63.60       +0.09\par   Ringgit         3.8000         3.8065       +0.17\par   Yuan            6.2087         6.2094       +0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.38         119.66       