\par\par \uc2 Asiastox\par \b \uc2 China Shares Fall Amid Doubts Over Beijing's Rescue\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gregor Stuart Hunter   \par \uc2 1,280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2015\par 03:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks fell Tuesday, casting doubt on the government's ability to stem the slide.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Beijing took its most aggressive action yet to boost its markets, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-setting-up-fund-to-stabilize-stock-market-1435991611"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspending initial public offerings }}}\uc2  and lending cash to investors to buy stocks. China's brokers vowed to buy shares until the Shanghai Composite hits the 4500 level.\par \par \uc2 But the market fell 1.3% Tuesday to 3727.12, putting it down 27.9% from its peak and 17.2% below the promised 4500 level. More worrying is that the market performed worse than the index makes it seem.\par \par \uc2 China's smaller Shenzhen stock market fell for the second straight day, putting it down 5.3% for the week while the ChiNext board, composed of smaller cap stocks, and dropped 11.2% to 2352.01. Both indexes are off more than a third from June highs.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's market also sank, with the \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  Index falling 1% and a gauge of Chinese companies listed offshore in the city, known as H-shares, falling 3.3% during the trading day to enter a bear market\u8212\'20\'14defined as a drop of more than 20%\u8212\'20\'14compared with highs reached in May.\par \par \uc2 The performance in Shanghai showed how government efforts to boost the market are playing out. Just 55 companies rose Tuesday while 864 names fell, according to Chinese data provider Wind Info. Those gainers were the market's heavyweights, which the brokers pledged to buy. Companies such as \uc2 Bank of China Ltd\uc2 ., \uc2 China Construction Bank Corp\uc2 . and \uc2 Ping An Insurance\uc2  (Group) Co. of China rose the maximum 10% trading limit.\par \par \uc2 Beijing's policy changes to stabilize the stock market seemed unlikely to produce a durable recovery, even if the market is able to rebound in the short term, said Arthur Kwong, head of Asia-Pacific equities at \uc2 BNP Paribas Investment Partners\uc2 , which has \u8364\'20\'AC548 billion ($605.86 billion) in assets under management. He says he remains wary of Chinese domestic shares even after the selloff during the past month.\par \par \uc2 "We'd only be excited when the market has a turnaround in terms of fundamentals," he said. What's more, policy moves so far have shown limited effectiveness in improving economic growth. "A lot of the bullets are already shot," he added. "How many more rate cuts can they do?"\par \par \uc2 Some analysts attribute Tuesday's losses in China to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/chinese-firms-discover-margin-lendings-downside-1435653636"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 margin calls }}}\uc2 , when brokerages call in money owed by investors who borrowed to buy shares. "The pressure on margin calls remain heavy," said Qian Qimin, an analyst at Shenyin Wanguo Securities. While some highly leveraged Chinese investors have already been forced to liquidate margin positions in small and midcap stocks, the selloff could continue.\par \par \uc2 "The entire clearance process, in our view, may last a few more weeks," said Nomura in a research report.\par \par \uc2 China has rolled out a steady stream of measures to arrest the selling frenzy that knocked $2.4 trillion in value from China's equities over the past three weeks. According to data from FactSet, 514 stocks are suspended in Shenzhen and 162 in Shanghai. Despite the recent rout, Shanghai shares are up 81% over the past year, and 15.2% since January. Shanghai recovered modestly Monday, which some investors and analysts attributed to heavy buying of blue-chip stocks by state-backed funds.\par \par \uc2 That buying looks set to continue. Chinese brokerage \uc2 Haitong Securities Co\uc2 . on Tuesday said it would boost the amount it invests in blue-chip exchange-traded funds by 15 billion yuan ($2.42 billion). The announcement follows an agreement over the weekend among 21 brokerages to invest in a stock-rescue fund.\par \par \uc2 Other measures include halting new initial public offerings, raising quotas for foreigners to buy stocks and an initiative by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide funds to help investors borrow to buy shares.\par \par \uc2 Some brokerages are encouraged by Beijing's efforts: "Chinese monetary and fiscal easing policies, combined with further reform measures, should support [mainland] A-share indexes to new highs in 2016," says Raymond So, co-head of research at Chinese broker CCB International Securities. A number of sectors stand to benefit from the Beijing-backed call to buy, including financials, property developers, health care, utilities and telecoms, he added.\par \par \uc2 Still, China's volatility is starting to spill into global markets, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/chinas-moves-to-rescue-its-stock-market-may-come-at-a-price-1436186850"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beijing's moves to arrest stock selloffs }}}\uc2  have darkened the outlook for the world's second-largest economy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/oil-prices-fall-to-3-month-low-on-china-iran-worries-1436175365"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oil prices tumbled nearly 8% Monday }}}\uc2 , their biggest single-day decline in more than three months, amid fresh fears about weaker demand from China, one of the world's largest consumers of raw materials. The sharp falls moderated Tuesday, with Brent crude gaining 1.6% to $57.43.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's market has risen strongly but was never gripped by the mania that sent Chinese stocks soaring. While it is considered a more mature market with far more institutional investors, Hong Kong has hundreds of mainland Chinese companies, mostly large state-owned banks and heavy-industry companies, which account for 44.1% of the market capitalization of all stocks listed on the city's exchange.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Asian markets mostly rose as investors appear hopeful that a resolution between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/solution-to-greek-crisis-wont-come-overnight-juncker-warns-1436255691"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greece and its creditors }}}\uc2 is still within reach.\par \par \uc2 "It seems that investors either believe that 'Grexit' can still be avoided, or that, if it does happen, the contagion will be limited," analysts from Capital Economics wrote in a research report.\par \par \uc2 Greece's vote on Sunday to reject creditors' demands, including pension cuts and tax increases, could put Greece closer to exiting the eurozone. That led markets in Europe and the U.S. lower, though the declines weren't as dramatic as expected. The euro fell 0.7% against the U.S. dollar and 0.5% against the yen.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 Stock Average rose 1.3% while South Korea's Kospi Composite fell 0.7%.\par \par \uc2 Australia's S&P/ASX 200 rose 1.9%, its strongest one-day gain since mid-February, with falling oil expected to lower operating costs for energy-intensive commodity producers. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  kept benchmark interest rates on hold at 2.00%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, banks warned that Malaysia's financial markets could come under further stress, after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/malaysias-ringgit-buckling-under-political-pressure-1436160213"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell to its weakest level since the Asian financial crisis }}}\uc2  Monday. The oil-exporting nation has been hit by falling commodity prices, which have nearly halved since July last year. Malaysia's stocks are down 1%.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit strengthened 0.3% to 3.8151 against the dollar amid speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buoy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. The ringgit is down 8.2% for the year, making it one of Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Among Asian financial assets, Malaysia's are the most exposed to oil," analysts from ING wrote in a research note. Efforts to strengthen the ringgit "will give way if oil prices continue to decline," the bank added.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has come under pressure as political strain builds against the country's prime minister. The Wall Street Journal earlier reported that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10130211234592774869404581083700187014570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Malaysian government investigators looking into the activities of state investment fund 1Malaysia Development Bhd }}}\uc2 ., or 1MDB, had traced almost $700 million in deposits into what they believe are Mr. Najib's personal accounts. Mr. Najib has denied wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Malaysian authorities said they have ordered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/malaysia-authorities-order-six-bank-accounts-frozen-tied-to-probe-of-alleged-transfers-to-prime-minister-najib-1436253593"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six bank accounts to be frozen }}}\uc2 in connection with an investigation into alleged fund transfers to bank accounts of Mr. Najib.\par \par \uc2 Anjie Zheng, Yifan Xie and Dominique Fong contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gregor Stuart Hunter at \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120150707eb770001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
