\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  slide as volatile China stocks, Greece hit sentiment\b0\par\par\uc2 774 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2015\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won near 4-month low as offshore funds sell\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -traders\par     * Rupiah near 2-week high ahead of bond auction\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 7 (Reuters) - South Korea's won slumped to\par near four-month lows on Tuesday, leading losses among emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as risk sentiment was hit by volatile Chinese\par stocks and caution ahead of a euro zone summit to ease Greece's\par debt crisis.\par     The Malaysian ringgit was steady after hitting a\par fresh 16-year low as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par stabilise the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, traders\par said. The Indonesian rupiah hit a near two-week high on\par bond inflows.\par     The won lost as much as 0.5 percent to 1,131.7\par per dollar, its weakest since March 17. Offshore funds unloaded\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as Seoul shares touched a near three-week\par low on foreign selling.\par     Chinese stocks continue to lose ground despite emergency\par support measures from Beijing, adding to a depressing backdrop\par for global risk markets. \par     Ahead of an emergency euro zone summit later in the day,\par France and Germany told Greece on Monday to come up with serious\par proposals in order to restart financial aid talks.\par  Greeks voted overwhelmingly to reject more\par austerity at a weekend referendum. \par     Investors clung to hopes the summit might yet find a way for\par Greece to ease its debt burden and stay in the euro zone. Still,\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to remain soft, traders and\par analysts said.\par     "The won could fall to hit 1,150 within the third quarter as\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to weaken further," said\par Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Seoul.\par     "It is reckless to bet amid uncertainties. We may see some\par positive developments on Greece tonight, but that will not erase\par all of the problems. China's steps on the economy and markets\par are not seen as being effective yet."\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit started down 0.1 percent at 3.8100 per dollar,\par its weakest since May 1999, Thomson Reuters data showed, as\par offshore funds continued to trim their exposure to the Malaysian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted aggressively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to stem losses in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said. The ringgit has\par lost 8.1 on the dollar so far this year - the steepest fall\par among Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the period. \par     Investors sold most government bonds, especially long-term\par debts. The 10-year yield briefly rose to 4.051\par percent, its highest since June 30 when \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  affirmed\par the country's credit rating and upgraded the outlook.\par .\par     The five-year yield also advanced to as high as\par 3.632 percent.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose 0.5 percent to 13,285 on the dollar, its\par strongest since June 24, as foreign investors picked up the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of a government bond auction later in the day.\par     Indonesia is hoping to raise 10 trillion rupiah ($751.9\par million) in the bond sale. Traders expect strong demand for the\par sale due to the prevailing higher yields.\par     On June 23, the rupiah rallied on bond inflows, bucking the\par downturn in regional peers.\par     The country sold 18 trillion rupiah worth of conventional\par bonds at an auction on the day, above an indicative target of 12\par trillion rupiah. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0625 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       122.69         122.58       -0.09\par   Sing dlr        1.3523         1.3485       -0.28\par   Taiwan dlr      30.960         31.150       +0.61\par   Korean won     1129.69        1126.50       -0.28\par   Baht             33.88          33.84       -0.12\par   Peso             45.13          45.10       -0.06\par   Rupiah        13285.00       13348.00       +0.47\par   Rupee            63.38          63.40       +0.03\par   Ringgit         3.8050         3.8065       +0.04\par   Yuan            6.2093         6.2092       -0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       122.69         119.66       -2.47\par   Sing dlr        1.3523         1.3260       -1.94\par   Taiwan dlr      30.960         31.718       +2.45\par   Korean won     1129.69        1099.30       -2.69\par   Baht             33.88          32.90       -2.90\par   Peso             45.13          44.72       -0.90\par   Rupiah        13285.00       12380.00       -6.81\par   Rupee            63.38          63.03       -0.56\par   Ringgit         3.8050         3.4965       -8.11\par   Yuan            6.2093         6.2040       -0.09\par   ($1 = 13,300 rupiah)\par \par  (Additional reporting by Reuters \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analyst Krishna Kumar in\par SYDNEY)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-7-7T08:26:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150707eb77008ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
