\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Risk aversion weighs on Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , won falls with  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 06:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won falls as S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted\par     * Ringgit down on corp dollar bids; higher oil cuts losses\par     * Rupiah skids, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limits slides\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, March 26 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on Thursday as military action against rebels\par in Yemen and losses on Wall Street undermined risk sentiment.\par     The South Korean won fell as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities were spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb its strength,\par traders said.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ringgit and Indonesia's rupiah \par slid on corporate dollar demand. The Philippine peso \par eased ahead of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy meeting later in the\par day when the authority is expected to keep interest rates\par unchanged. \par     Asian stocks skidded as Saudi Arabia and its Gulf Arab\par allies started a military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Yemen. \par U.S. equities on Wednesday also lost ground with the Nasdaq\par  suffering its largest decline in nearly a year.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed muted reactions to the dollar's\par weakness after data showing spending on U.S. durable goods fell\par for a sixth consecutive month in February. \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw more impact from risk aversion than\par the dollar," said Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "However, they may find some relief as money printing in \par China and Japan, as well as stabilisation in major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par could spur more carry trades in Asia," Park added.\par     \par     WON\par     The won fell as South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities\par were spotted defending the 1,100 per dollar level, traders said.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has chart resistance levels at\par 1,099.7, a 55-day moving average and 1,099.4, a 100-day moving\par average. The unit has been closing the local daily market weaker\par than the 100-day average since Sept. 5.\par     "From 1,100, the authorities was suspected of pulling up\par (dollar/won)," said a foreign bank trader in Seoul.\par     The authorities were also seen keeping the won weaker than\par 9.2000 against the yen, traders said.\par     The won weakened to near 9.3000 to the yen from the previous\par close of 9.2110. South Korea and Japan compete in overseas\par markets for various products such as electronics and cars.\par     Meanwhile, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it boosted the ceiling on\par its key loan facility for small-to-medium sized businesses by\par 5.0 trillion won as part of its push to boost the economic\par recovery at home. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slid on quarter-end dollar demand from local\par companies.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its losses as oil\par prices jumped. The Saudi Arabia-led strike on Yemen rebels could\par pose risks to the security of oil shipments.\par     Malaysia is a net oil exporter and the recent slide in crude\par prices boosted concerns over their impact on the country's\par current and fiscal accounts.\par     Given those worries, the ringgit was the worst-performing\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year with a near 5 percent loss\par against the dollar, Thomson Reuters data showed.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah skidded with month-end corporate dollar demand\par increasing.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,003 rupiah per dollar, weaker\par than Wednesday's 12,932.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expects the rupiah to remain under\par pressure through June as dollar demand rises for dividend\par payments, its chief said on Wednesday. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par ailing unit, but the official support was not seen as\par aggressive, traders said.\par     "It just gave some liquidity for the market," said a\par Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader.\par     Providing some long-term relief was news Japanese companies\par will invest $5.6 billion in Indonesia, the head of Indonesia's\par investment board said, following President Joko Widodo's visit\par to Tokyo. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0500 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.98         119.50       +0.44\par   Sing dlr        1.3693         1.3708       +0.11\par   Taiwan dlr      31.300         31.401       +0.32\par   Korean won     1104.90        1100.80       -0.37\par   Baht             32.58          32.55       -0.09\par   Peso             44.84          44.76       -0.18\par   Rupiah        13010.00       12982.00       -0.22\par   Rupee            62.63          62.33       -0.48\par   Ringgit         3.6750         3.6660       -0.24\par   Yuan            6.2145         6.2125       -0.03\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.98         119.66       +0.57\par   Sing dlr        1.3693         1.3260       -3.16\par   Taiwan dlr      31.300         31.718       +1.34\par   Korean won     1104.90        1099.30       -0.51\par   Baht             32.58          32.90       +0.98\par   Peso             44.84          44.72       -0.26\par   Rupiah        13010.00       12380.00       -4.84\par   Rupee            62.63          63.03       +0.64\par   Ringgit         3.6750         3.4965       -4.86\par   Yuan            6.2145         6.2040       -0.17\par  \par  (Additional reporting by KyoungHo Lee in SEOUL; Editing by)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-26T06:45:13.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150326eb3q0063v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
