\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won turns up after 20-month low as further rate cut views wane\b0\par\par\uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won ends up as no further S.Korea rate cut seen in 2015\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  lowers rates to record low 1.75 pct\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution supports most emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds detail, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, March 12 (Reuters) - South Korea's won ended\par local trade firmer, recovering slightly  from a 20-month trough\par hit on Thursday when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly slashed\par borrowing costs to a record low.\par     Expectations of another interest rate cut anytime soon\par vanished, with a snap Reuters poll of analysts finding the\par surprise cut now viewed as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's last easing, at\par least for this year. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  slashed its base rate by 25\par basis points to 1.75 percent at its monthly policy meeting.\par  \par     The won closed at 1,126.4 per dollar after\par falling to 1,136.4 per dollar, its weakest since July 10, 2013,\par compared with Wednesday's close of 1,126.5. \par     Traders rushed to cover the short positions they had built\par up on expectations of further easing, and treasury bond futures\par  pared back much of their gains they made after the rate\par cut. \par     Finance Minister Choi Kyung-hwan told reporters after a\par scheduled meeting that Thursday's rate cut was a pre-emptive\par move and would help revive the economy. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 's rate cut is unlikely to spur sharp\par portfolio outflows as foreign investors have been happy to\par accumulate Korean debt, said Jonathan Cavenagh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     "However, as the U.S. gets closer to raising rates the\par attractiveness of investing in Korean debt may start to become\par more questionable," he added.\par     Meanwhile, most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose as caution\par set in over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities to stem\par excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ringgit gained as nerves over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prompted investors\par to cover short positions.\par     Traders scrambled for the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when it\par strengthened past 3.6900 per dollar.\par     The government has sold 4.0 billion ringgit ($1.1 billion)\par in bonds maturing in 2025 with bid-to-cover ratio of 2.23 times\par at an average yield of 3.955 percent, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said\par earlier. \par     Most government bond prices and Kuala Lumpur shares \par rose.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The Thai baht edged up even though the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of\par Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  unexpectedly cut borrowing costs on Wednesday.\par  \par     The baht slid to as low as 32.92 per dollar earlier on\par Thursday, its weakest since Jan. 7.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firmed, analysts said, because the rate\par reduction is unlikely to undercut the baht against regional\par peers.\par     "We do not think this knee-jerk reaction to the rate cut\par will necessarily cause the THB to reverse all of its recent\par outperformance versus most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Dominic\par Bunning, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in a client note.\par     The baht has gained 0.1 percent against the dollar so far\par this year, making it the third best-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par according to Thomson Reuters data.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0610 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.32         121.46       +0.12\par   Sing dlr        1.3834         1.3888       +0.39\par   Taiwan dlr      31.615         31.666       +0.16\par   Korean won     1126.30        1126.50       +0.02\par   Baht             32.84          32.90       +0.18\par   Peso             44.26          44.34       +0.18\par   Rupiah        13190.00       13186.00       -0.03\par   Rupee            62.52          62.78       +0.42\par   Ringgit         3.6840         3.6970       +0.35\par   Yuan            6.2629         6.2623       -0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.32         119.66       -1.37\par   Sing dlr        1.3834         1.3260       -4.15\par   Taiwan dlr      31.615         31.718       +0.33\par   Korean won     1126.30        1099.30       -2.40\par   Baht             32.84     