\par\par \b \uc2 USD/MYR Hits 5.5-Year High, Eyes 3.6000 Barrier -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2015\par 07:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0610 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Malaysia's ringgit has chalked up a 5.5-year low of 3.5950 to the U.S. dollar as the price of Brent crude oil fell 1.1% to $46.08 a barrel. The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 2.8/% against the dollar this year. In the last two months of 2014, the ringgit depreciated 5.9% due to oil prices collapsing. The USD/MYR psychological trading barrier of 3.6000, if breached, could trigger stoploss orders to sell more ringgit. \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a sharp fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but according to one onshore trader, this seems less likely given \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  has not been active in the spot market recently. The USD/MYR is now at 3.5950 versus its Tuesday close of 3.5920. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: FLS\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 14-01-15 0626GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150114eb1e00078\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
