\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit, rupiah lowest since 2008/09 crisis, Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  down on U.S., China data\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2014\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices. For midday report, double-click\par  )\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 8 (Reuters) - Malaysia's ringgit and\par Indonesia's rupiah hit their weakest since the 2008-09 global\par financial crisis on Monday, as emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost\par ground after solid U.S. job data boosted the chance of an early\par Federal Reserve interest rate hike.    \par     Regional units also came under pressure as China's November\par imports unexpectedly shrank and exports growth eased, increasing\par fears of a sharp slowdown in the world's second-largest economy.\par .\par     The Chinese yuan turned weaker despite the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  setting a stronger official guidance rate. \par     The ringgit lost as much as 0.9 percent to 3.5040\par per dollar, its weakest since September 2009, on worries that\par lower oil prices would hurt Malaysia's current account and\par fiscal deficits.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit\par depreciation in the worst-performing emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so\par far this year, traders said.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market are aimed at\par ensuring orderly market conditions," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  told\par Reuters in an email.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility was likely to persist until the energy\par and commodity markets stabilise and a stronger recovery occurs\par in the major advanced economies, it added.\par     The rupiah fell 0.6 percent to 12,365 per dollar,\par its weakest since November 2008, on year-end dollar demand from\par local companies.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its earlier losses after\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it is conducting "measured\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " to support the unit. \par     Thailand's baht weakened past psychological support\par at 33.00 per dollar to hit its weakest since January, when\par political tensions hit local financial markets.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0805 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.20         121.53       +0.27\par   Sing dlr        1.3228         1.3226       -0.02\par   Taiwan dlr      31.280         31.192       -0.28\par   Korean won     1116.77        1114.10       -0.24\par   Baht             33.07          32.89       -0.54\par  *Peso             44.54          44.54       +0.00\par   Rupiah        12348.00       12295.00       -0.43\par   Rupee            61.94          61.77       -0.27\par   Ringgit         3.4940         3.4710       -0.66\par   Yuan            6.1637         6.1502       -0.22\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.20         105.28      -13.14\par   Sing dlr        1.3228         1.2632   