\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Global economic recovery signs lift Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , yuan jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 943 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2014\par 06:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won near 6-year high on stock inflows; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limits\par     * Baht gains to pre-coup level on offshore, local investors\par     * Ringgit around 7-month high as hedge funds buy NDFs\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 9 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose\par on Monday as U.S. and China data pointed to a strengthening\par global economic recovery, while the yuan jumped after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed the daily midpoint surprisingly higher.\par     The South Korean won touched a near six-year peak\par on sustained stock inflows, although \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities capped its upside.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ringgit hit a near seven-month high,\par tracking its strength in non-deliverable forwards (NDFs)\par  on hedge funds demand.\par     The Thai baht advanced to levels seen before the\par May 22 military coup on demand from both offshore and local\par investors as public protests against the junta dwindled.\par  \par     U.S jobs data on Friday showed nonfarm payrolls increased\par 217,000 last month, bringing employment back to its\par pre-recession level and validating the view that labour\par conditions are improving. \par     In China, exports in May gained steam, even though an\par unexpected drop in imports indicated weaker domestic demand in\par the world's second-largest economy, weekend data showed.\par  \par     Those signs of global recovery came as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week eased its monetary policy to prevent deflation in\par the euro zone.\par     With those policy step, investors have been expected to\par chase higher-yielding assets in emerging Asia.\par     "The U.S. nonfarm payrolls data came in at a 'sweet spot'\par for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Scotiabank said in a client note.\par     "This combined with the Chinese trade data over the weekend\par has set a positive tone for EM Asia at the outset of the week,\par and should help bolster even underperforming Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par it added. \par     \par     WON\par     The won advanced 0.3 percent to 1,017.0 per dollar, its\par strongest since August 2008, as foreign investors were set to\par extend their buying spree in Seoul shares for an 18th\par consecutive session.\par     They have bought a combined net 3.15 trillion won ($3.10\par billion) worth of stocks during the period, the Korea Exchange\par data showed.\par     The won also found support from catch-up demand as South\par Korean financial markets were closed on Friday for a holiday\par when other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained on the ECB's easing and a\par stronger yuan.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were, however, spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the won's appreciation as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also\par hit a near six-year high against the Japanese yen.\par     South Korea's major companies compete with Japanese peers in\par key overseas markets and industries.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht rose as much as 0.5 percent to 32.42 per dollar,\par its strongest since May 22 when Thailand's military seized \par power.\par     Army chief and coup leader General Prayuth Chan-ocha on\par Saturday declared himself the head of the Board of Investment,\par paving the way for the approval of a 700 billion baht ($21.6\par billion) pending investment projects.\par     The number of protesters against the coup also dwindled\par although the junta kept thousands of troops and police ready to\par deal with any public demonstrations. \par     Last week, foreign investors bought a combined net 8.04\par billion baht in Bangkok shares.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose as much as 0.6 percent to 3.1930 per\par dollar, its strongest since Nov. 21.\par     Hedge funds bought one-month NDFs, traders\par said.\par     A senior Malaysian bank trader in Kuala Lumpur said spot\par ringgit has room to strengthen to 3.1700-3.1800.\par     Malaysian exports surged by nearly a fifth in April, beating\par market forecasts and increasing expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may raise interest rates next month. \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah gained on its strength in overnight NDFs\par  market.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate, which\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched last year in an effort to\par manage exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 11,790 per\par dollar, stronger than the previous day's 11,823.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, gave up some of earlier\par gains on dollar demand linked to dividend payments, traders\par said.\par     The rupiah NDFs on Monday turned slightly weaker on renewed\par worries about the country's current account deficit and\par uncertainty over July's presidential election.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0435 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.50         102.47       -0.03\par   Sing dlr        1.2508         1.2517       +0.07\par   Taiwan dlr      30.003         30.080       +0.26\par   Korean won     1017.10        1020.50       +0.33\par   Baht             32.43          32.57       +0.43\par   Peso             43.59          43.65       +0.15\par   Rupiah        11780.00       11830.00       +0.42\par   Rupee            59.03          59.17       +0.23\par   Ringgit         3.1960         3.2120       +0.50\par   Yuan            6.2384         6.2502       +0.19\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.50         105.28       +2.71\par   Sing dlr        1.2508         1.2632       +0.99\par   Taiwan dlr      30.003         29.950       -0.18\par   Korean won     1017.10        1055.40       +3.77\par   Baht             32.43          32.86       +1.33\par   Peso             43.59          44.40       +1.86\par   Rupiah        11780.00       12160.00       +3.23\par   Rupee            59.03          61.80       +4.69\par   Ringgit         3.1960         3.2755       +2.49\par   Yuan            6.2384         6.0539       -2.96\par   ($1 = 32.42 baht)\par   ($1 = 1017.1 won)\par \par  (Additional reporting by Satawasin Staporncharnchai IN BANGKOK;\par Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-9T05:54:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140609ea69003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
