\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Indonesia trade deficit hits rupiah; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2014\par 07:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Indonesia Apr trade balance at -$1.97 bln vs +$0.22 f'cast\par     * Won falls on foreign selling, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution\par     * Ringgit slides as stocks underperform\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 2 (Reuters) - The rupiah hit its weakest\par level in more than three months on Monday after Indonesia\par unexpectedly reported a trade deficit, leading losses among\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as investors took profits on May's\par gains amid broad strength in the dollar.\par     Regional units came under further pressure as the Australian\par dollar was hit by data showing Australian building\par approvals in April fell more than expected. \par     The South Korean won fell as foreign investors\par sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem its appreciation.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ringgit slid on weaker domestic stocks\par .\par     "The market appeared to adjust positions on the Australian\par dollar's weakness," said Jeong My-young, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures'\par research head in Seoul.\par     "Still, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have more positive factors given a\par recovery in China's economy and the ECB's further easing," Jeong\par added.\par     Chinese factory activity expanded at the fastest pace in\par five months in May due to rising new orders, official data\par showed on Sunday, increasing hopes that the economy is regaining\par momentum in the second quarter. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to deliver economic\par stimulus on Thursday via monetary easing.\par     The speculation has caused investors to seek higher yields\par in emerging Asia, helping most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  enjoy monthly\par gains.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah fell as much as 0.7 percent to 11,750\par per dollar, its weakest since Feb. 24.\par     Indonesia reported a surprise $1.97 billion trade deficit in\par April, against the market forecast of a $0.22 billion surplus\par and following two consecutive months of surpluses, official data\par showed earlier. \par     The rupiah is seen staying weaker in June as inflationary\par pressure and imports could pick up on rising consumption ahead\par of Ramadan, traders said.\par     A Jakarta-based trader said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may also come under\par pressure from dollar demand linked to dividend payments.\par     \par     WON\par     The won slid as mounting caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par caused investors to cut holdings in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Last week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were spotted\par buying dollars to prevent the won from strengthening beyond\par 1,020 to the greenback, traders said.\par     Foreign investors bought dollars in the futures market,\par traders said.\par     South Korean exports in May suffered their worst decline in\par eight months due to a drop in Chinese demand and fewer working\par days. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell as Kuala Lumpur shares lost 0.6\par percent, underperforming most regional stock markets.\par     Investors also covered dollar-short positions on the\par Australian dollar's slide.\par     Still, traders expected the ECB's potential easing to\par support the ringgit, as the monetary policy may spur more\par capital inflows to Asia.\par     "It is just market squaring up for mega events this week\par such as the ECB meeting," said a senior Malaysian bank trader in\par Kuala Lumpur, referring to the ringgit's daily loss.\par     The trader said he was looking to buy the ringgit around\par 3.2350 per dollar on dips.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0505 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.02         101.79       -0.23\par   Sing dlr        1.2558         1.2548       -0.08\par  *Taiwan dlr      30.042         30.050       +0.03\par   Korean won     1024.00        1020.10       -0.38\par   Baht             32.86          32.85       -0.02\par   Peso             43.86          43.76       -0.23\par   Rupiah        11750.00       11670.00       -0.68\par   Rupee            59.08          59.10       +0.03\par   Ringgit         3.2240         3.2130       -0.34\par  *Yuan            6.2473         6.2473       +0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.02         105.28       +3.19\par   Sing dlr        1.2558         1.2632       +0.59\par   Taiwan dlr      30.042         29.950       -0.31\par   Korean won     1024.00        1055.40       +3.07\par   Baht             32.86          32.86       +0.02\par   Peso             43.86          44