\par\par \b \uc2 Ringgit Stable Near 4-Year Low on Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2014\par 02:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0158 GMT [Dow Jones] The \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  ringgit is hovering near its 4-year low of MYR3.3465 to the U.S. dollar even as the greenback rallies higher against other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to intensifying risk aversion. USD/MYR is struggling to make headway; market participants speculate that strong 'sell' orders around 3.3470 might be a sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically exerts its influence in the spot market via a select few banks, making it relatively easy for traders to deduce when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The daily chart suggests potential for the dollar to hit 3.3730 - the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel - if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps away from capping USD/MYR. The Bollinger uptrend channel is a statistics-based technical analysis tool that charts a likely path of future price movement by extrapolating from the amplitude of recent fluctuations. USD/MYR is now 3.3445 from its last close of 3.3450. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 03, 2014 20:58 ET (01:58 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140204ea240008b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
