\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains; ringgit higher before budget\b0\par\par\uc2 967 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2013\par 03:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah to see best week since Sept 2009 on inflows * \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  PM Najib's budget speech eyed * Won dips on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution, exporters limit losses (Adds text, updates prices) By Jongwoo Cheon SINGAPORE, ct 25 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit a near eight-week high on Friday, leading gains among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will maintain its bond-buying programme through early next year kept the dollar pressured. The rupiah is poised to enjoy the best week in more than four years on capital inflows and demand from real money funds. The Malaysian ringgit gained on hopes the government will announce later in the day measures to cut the fiscal deficit. The dollar stayed around a nine-month low against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a disappointing U.S. jobs data earlier this week cemented views that the Fed's plans to taper its stimulus won't start until next year.\par \par \uc2  "With the market pushing out the timing of Fed tapering until March 2014, further portfolio inflows into emerging Asia can be expected in the near-term," ANZ said in a client note. Even before the U.S. September payrolls number, most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had gravitated to the view that the recently-ended 16-day \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  shutdown will likely prompt the Fed to delay a shift in policy.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah took top honours in emerging Asia this week,\par making the most out of the dollar's dour near term outlook.   \par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has risen 3.0 percent against the\par dollar, the largest weekly gain since the week ended on June 5,\par 2009, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par     The rupiah is seen as one of the most vulnerable to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed's tapering due to Indonesia's sizable current account deficit. It remains the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the year. Last week, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Agus Martowardojo said the current account deficit is likely to ease to less than 3 percent of gross domestic product. The gap hit 4.4 percent in the second quarter. The ringgit has also gained 0.4 percent so far this week, while the Taiwan dollar has risen 0.2 percent. The Singapore dollar is up 0.1 percent. The South Korean won took a different path, turning weaker for the week with a 0.1 percent loss after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities on Thursday were spotted buying dollars after earlier warning against "excessive" won moves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose as much as 1.6 percent to 10,970 per dollar,\par its strongest since Sept. 2, on demand from custodian banks.\par     The forward onshore market, or Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar\par Rate (JISDOR), was fixed at 11,142 per dollar,\par compared with Thursday's 11,268.\par     Five-year Indonesian government bond yield fell\par to 6.896 percent, the lowest since July 10. Three-year yield\par  also slid to 6.631 percent, the lowest since June 25.\par     Domestic shares eased, but the market enjoyed\par foreign buying in the previous two sessions.\par     A Jakarta-based trader said the rupiah may strengthen to\par 10,700.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit advanced on hopes that the government may\par announce steps to tackle Malaysia's fiscal deficit when Prime\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  unveils the 2014 budget.\par     "Our fundamental view is mildly bullish on the budget and we\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expect price to head towards 3.0770 should the budget meet expectations," Maybank said, referring to the ringgit's value to the dollar, in a note. Still, local investors took profits to guard against any disappointment from the prime minister's proposals. The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a chart resistance at 3.1410, a 200-day moving average.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     WON\par     The won edged down as offshore funds sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par heightened caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par authorities.\par     Foreign investors were poised to report their first selling\par day in Seoul's main stock market in 41 sessions.\par     Still, the won found relief from exporters' month-end demand\par for settlements, traders said.\par     South Korea's economy grew 1.1 percent in the third quarter\par from the previous three months, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  estimated,\par slightly beating market expectations. \par     "The authorities are likely to keep the won around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 current level. The won's resistance is seen firmer if foreigners stop a buying spree in the stock market," said a foreign bank trader in Seoul. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0430 GMT\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        97.01          97.29       +0.29\par   Sing dlr        1.2372         1.2374       +0.02\par   Taiwan dlr      29.401         29.452       +0.17\par   Korean won     1061.90        1061.00       -0.08\par   Baht             31.14          31.16       +0.08\par   Peso             43.07          43.09       +0.05\par   Rupiah        10975.00       11140.00       +1.50\par   Rupee            61.54          61.46       -0.13\par   Ringgit         3.1455         3.1605       +0.48\par   Yuan            6.0823         6.0820       -0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2013\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        97.01          86.79      -10.53\par   Sing dlr        1.2372         1.2219       -1.24\par   Taiwan dlr      29.401         29.136       -0.90\par   Korean won     1061.90        1070.60       +0.82\par   Baht             31.14          30.61       -1.69\par   Peso             43.07          41.05       -4.69\par   Rupiah        10975.00        9630.00      -12.26\par   Rupee            61.54          54.99      -10.64\par   Ringgit         3.1455         3.0580       -2.78\par   Yuan            6.0823         6.2303       +2.43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by KyoungHo Lee in SEOUL and IFR Markets' Catherine Tan; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | IF | J | M | PHD | SNI | SI | Z | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131028e9ap0001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
