ut of emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1200 (psychological support), then at 6.1135 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1090 (record low). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1221 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1302 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1386 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - consolidation with possible upside bias. Signs of an upside break may be appearing in USD/TWD, which is on the edge of crossing the 20-day Bollinger mid and also above the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. A Thursday close above 30.060 might lend a bullish tone to USD/TWD and set it on a path toward the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 30.180. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield slipping a bit lower overnight could however mean that the dollar may trade with a slightly offered tone, and that could keep USD/TWD trapped within its recent range of 29.900-30.130. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.000 (psychological support), then at 29.990 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 29.950 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.060 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.180 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - downside bias. USD/KRW gaps lower open at 1,113 from its Wednesday close of 1,115.4, as investor sentiment improves overnight. USD/KRW could be headed lower if it ends Thursday below 1,113 and therefore within the bearish pull of the Bollinger downtrend channel. A break of the 1,110 psychological support could trigger more selling related to stoploss orders and push the dollar to the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,108. The change in risk appetite can best be seen in the Kospi, which is up 0.6% and leading the way for Asia thus far. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,113 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,110 (psychological support), before 1,108 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,118 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1,120 (psychological resistance), before 1,121 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - consolidation. USD/SGD dropped out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, as the dollar eased on the back of the decline in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield - which resulted from investors' flight to quality assets. USD/SGD could be consolidating in a lower range of 1.2718-1.2791 demarcated by the 20-day Bollinger mid support and the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel. The Singapore dollar, being a regional anchor, may also be benefiting from a reallocation of money from riskier South East Asia countries such as Indonesia and Malaysia, where their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have depreciated sharply over the last month, into Singapore. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2750 (psychological support), then at 1.2719 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2700 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2791 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2865 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - pullback lower, upside bias to remain. USD/MYR is retreating to the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel as the dollar slips on improving investor sentiment. The dollar could hence find a base at 3.3045 but if it remains above this key level by the end of the day, the technical upside bias will remain. U.S. 10-year Treasury yields declining, as investors rush back into the traditional safe haven assets, may be pressuring the greenback slightly lower as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3045 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3000 (psychological support), before 3.2800 (psychological support and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 3.3350 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud), then at 3.3375 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3500 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - consolidation, possible pullback lower. USD/THB could be running out of upwards momentum for now, noting the doji candlestick pattern formed Wednesday. The dollar is a tad weaker across the board due to improving sentiment sparked by the relief rally in equities. USD/THB may decline toward the psychological support at 32.00 but the larger uptrend is not likely to be negated unless the pair falls below 31.62 and therefore exits the Bollinger uptrend channel. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.95 (daily Bollinger band standard deviation 2), before 31.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.28 (Wednesday's 3-year high), before 32.49 (monthly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP - possible pullback lower. USD/PHP may experience a profit-taking selloff as the pair now looks very much overbought on the daily chart - price action has been way above the upper Bollinger band (standard deviation 2) for the past four sessions. The dollar is weaker in Asia Thursday as a relief rally takes place in stocks and South East Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.50 (psychological support), then at 44.20 (psychological support), before 44.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.80 (psychological resistance), then at 45.00 (psychological resistance), before 45.21 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation lower. A pullback in dollar strength appears to be the theme of the day for South East Asia, as investor sentiment improves and stocks in Asia mount a relief rally. The rupiah could hence get a reprieve and recover toward 10,800 to the dollar. A key indicator to watch in order to gauge sentiment for the rupiah is whether the USD/IDR NDF premium subsides. The premium that the 1-month USD/IDR NDF contract commands over the spot price traded to almost IDR800 Wednesday, a sign that dollar liquidity in the onshore market is still thin and investor confidence is low. If this NDF premium falls to below IDR500, there could be more follow through in the rupiah recovery. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,900 (psychological support), then at 10,800 (psychological support), before 10,790 (daily Bollinger band standard deviation 2). Immediate resistance is at 11,000 (major psychological barrier), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - consolidation lower. The rupee could enjoy a brief relief rally as the dollar weakens broadly in Asia Thursday. The market is almost getting used to new record lows being set for the INR, especially with talk of a 100.00 USD/INR call option recently traded in the market - a bet that the rupee could fall to 100 to the dollar. The rupee last closed at 68.80 - the second consecutive record low this week. Investors have been especially bearish the rupee as the rapid depreciation has raised the possibility of capital flight from India. Though the government said last week there are no plans to install capital controls, India has a poor track record of consistency in its policy, hence rupee investors are still jittery and looking to take their money out while they can. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 68.50 (psychological support), then at 68.00 (psychological support), before 67.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 69.00(psychological resistance), before 70.00 (major psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write