\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CHAT: Malaysia ringgit steadies ahead of BOP data...\b0\par\par\uc2 1,498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2013\par 04:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 due 1000GMT which might show the country falling into a current account deficit for the first time since 1997. Technical analysis suggests the pair has an upside bias within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, potentially to the major psychological trading barrier at 3.3000. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, and will likely do so as well today, to slow the pace of ringgit depreciation. Bank Negara appears to be defending the 3.3000 psychological barrier as the ringgit is already at a 3-year low. The ringgit has been falling on speculation that shrinking exports will throw the country into the list of countries with a current account deficit - along with the likes of Indonesia and India. USD/MYR is now 3.2900. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0218 GMT [Dow Jones] A better-than-expected price performance in gold surprised her and the market, Helen Lau, a senior analyst at UOB Kay Hian, says in a report. She notes that positive catalysts for gold prices are better-than-expected physical demand in China, inflows into gold exchange-traded funds, strength of the USD and the impact of winding down of liquidity by the U.S. Federal Reserve. She also notes that some of UOB's clients are "tempted" to add exposure to gold via ETFs. "They are searching for positive catalysts or contrarian view on gold," Lau says. Spot gold is at $1,372/oz, up $1 from its previous close. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0206 GMT [Dow Jones] Base metal prices could have mostly risen in the past few days more due to short covering and Chinese demand not yet decelerating as expected, rather than on some supportive news, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  analysts say in a report. However, news of mines supply disruptions in copper have come at a time when Chinese imports of the metal has been rising, they say. "The issue with rising mine supply in the later part of 2013 is still relevant and copper is likely to exit the year in surplus, in our view," they add. Going forward, besides the release of the minutes of the Federal Reserve's July 30-31 meeting later in the global trading day, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's China manufacturing data for August could provide fresh cues to investors. LME 3-month copper is $7,299/ton, down $21, while aluminum is at $1,916/ton, up $1.50 from its previous close. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 on news that Japan raises severity of latest Fukushima leak to level 3, tilting the intraday technical bias negative. Further downside in the dollar/yen pair may encounter support at 96.91 on its hourly chart. The spot USD/JPY is last at 97.23. (jerry.tan@waj.com)\par \par \uc2 which resulted from a selloff in the greenback ahead of the July FOMC minutes due later in the global day. The USD/SGD is rising back toward Tuesday's 1.5-month high of 1.2799, guided by the Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports at 1.2735. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators are primed for a slightly hawkish tone in the minutes from the Fed's last meeting, and have likely positioned themselves long-dollars. The risk, therefore, is that the Fed turns out to be less hawkish than expected, which would result in a USD selloff again. The USD/SGD is now at 1.2763. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 as the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  monetary policy decision looms. The baht remains on a weak footing, after having hit a 1-year high of 31.72 Tuesday, as the technical bias remains for a stronger dollar. The USD/THB is likely to continue rising as long as it stays above 31.34 - the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel. Most analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the benchmark interest rate at 2.50%, even though export growth has been flagging and creating a drag on the economy. The BOT last cut the base lending rate by 25 basis points in May. The USD/THB is now at 31.70.(ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW falls to 1,117.0 vs 1,120.8 late Tuesday in Seoul, as investors waited to hear more on the future of the U.S. Federal Reserve's easy monetary policy. "U.S Treasury yields have fallen and the dollar has turned to weaken against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the broad market sentiment is still shaky," says a local bank dealer. Woori Futures analyst Son Eun-jeong tips the USD/KRW to be in a range of 1112 to 1120 for the session. (in-soo.nam@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0044 GMT [Dow Jones] A sharp fall in the Nikkei Stock Average on Tuesday has put it close to a level consistent with the USD/JPY's rate as stock prices have been relatively overvalued compared with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate level, says Junya Tanase, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  in Tokyo. He says the stock level matching with the USD/JPY rate, calculated at 97.28, is around 13,200 amid a strong correlation between them. "The USD/JPY's direction may eventually hinge on the stock market's moves, and may shrug off developments on U.S. interest rates after the release of the FOMC minutes later" in the global day, Tanase adds. The benchmark Nikkei 225 index ended at 13,396 on Tuesday. It opened 0.3% higher at 13,431.28. The USD/JPY rises to 97.50 vs 97.26 in late New York Tuesday.(tatsuo.ito@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 The USD/JPY is moderately higher due to buying from some investors and a slight gain in the Nikkei Stock Average, says a dealer at a Japanese bank; "the gain is flows-driven." The pair may rise as high as 98.00 in Asia as it broke through minor resistance of 97.50. The USD/JPY is at 97.54 vs 97.26 late New York Tuesday. But a sharper rise is unlikely as exporters could start selling dollars above 98.00, he adds. Attention is paid to whether Asian stock markets and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Indian rupee will recover after their recent falls, he adds.(tatsuo.ito@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 A lift in New Zealand's "net migration reflects the diverging economic outlooks between Australia and New Zealand," says ASB Senior Economist Jane Turner. While over the past year much of the increase in net migration was to Canterbury as the earthquake rebuild progressed, "more recently, the lift in net migration has been more broad based across the country, and this likely relates more to the poor economic performance and weak labour market in Australia," she says. The increase is a "development for the RBNZ to watch closely" as it will add further to housing demand when supply is low, Turner says. She expects the RBNZ's high loan-to-value lending restrictions "will only have a modest impact" and still sees the RBNZ starting to lift the cash rate from March 2014. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 A lift in New Zealand's "net migration reflects the diverging economic outlooks between Australia and New Zealand," says ASB Senior Economist Jane Turner. While over the past year much of the increase in net migration was to Canterbury as the earthquake rebuild progressed, "more recently, the lift in net migration has been more broad based across the country, and this likely relates more to the poor economic performance and weak labour market in Australia," she says. The increase is a "development for the RBNZ to watch closely" as it will add further to housing demand when supply is low, Turner says. She expects the RBNZ's high loan-to-value lending restrictions "will only have a modest impact" and still sees the RBNZ starting to lift the cash rate from March 2014. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2357 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude oil prices fall slightly in early Asian trading with investor attention fixated on the release of the minutes of the Federal Reserve's July 30-31 meeting and the weekly crude stocks data from the \uc2 U.S. Energy Information Administration\uc2 , both due later in the global trading day. Analysts surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires expect crude stocks to fall by 1.3 million barrels, even as refinery \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop by 0.4 percentage point. The supplies at Cushing, Oklahoma - a major hub - will represent the "most important number within the data," oil trading advisory firm Ritterbusch & Associates, says in a report. Going forward, HSBC China manufacturing data for August will a "more important driver," the company says. October Nymex crude is at $105.05 a barrel, down 6 cents from its previous close.(arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 20, 2013 22:20 ET (02:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130821e98l000kj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
